('10554', '2449', '_wp_attached_file', '2026/06/NYU-project-Image1.webp'),
('10555', '2449', '_wp_attachment_metadata', 'a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:706;s:6:\"height\";i:397;s:4:\"file\";s:31:\"2026/06/NYU-project-Image1.webp\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:29078;s:5:\"sizes\";a:2:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:31:\"NYU-project-Image1-300x169.webp\";s:5:\"width\";i:300;s:6:\"height\";i:169;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/webp\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:11074;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:31:\"NYU-project-Image1-150x150.webp\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/webp\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:5358;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:12:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:1:\"0\";s:6:\"credit\";s:0:\"\";s:6:\"camera\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:1:\"0\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:1:\"0\";s:3:\"iso\";s:1:\"0\";s:13:\"shutter_speed\";s:1:\"0\";s:5:\"title\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"orientation\";s:1:\"0\";s:8:\"keywords\";a:0:{}}}'),
('10556', '2449', '_source_url', 'https://www.ninjatropic.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/NYU-project-Image1.webp'),
('10557', '2446', '_thumbnail_id', '2447'),
('10558', '2446', 'client_name', 'NYU Langone Health'),
('10559', '2446', '_client_name', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_client_name'),
('10560', '2446', 'client_intro', '<p>NYU Langone Health is a leader in medical research and patient care. They embarked on a groundbreaking project to demystify near-death experiences (NDEs) for patients who have undergone cardiac arrest, combining cutting-edge research with compassionate patient communication.</p>'),
('10561', '2446', '_client_intro', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_client_intro'),
('10562', '2446', 'client_logo', '2448'),
('10563', '2446', '_client_logo', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_client_logo'),
('10564', '2446', 'challenge_title', 'Simplifying the Complex with Patient Education Videos'),
('10565', '2446', '_challenge_title', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_challenge_title'),
('10566', '2446', 'challenge', '<p>Near-death experiences — the vivid perceptions reported by patients following cardiac arrest — sit at a uniquely difficult intersection of science, psychology, and personal belief. Patients who survive cardiac arrest often carry confusion, fear, or spiritual distress about what they experienced. Healthcare providers lacked standardized materials to help patients contextualize these experiences within a medical framework.</p>
<p>NYU Langone needed educational content that was simultaneously grounded in Dr. Sam Parnia\'s peer-reviewed research, accessible to patients across a wide age and literacy range, and delivered in a tone that felt supportive rather than clinical or dismissive. The wrong approach — too cold, too simple, or too ambiguous — risked undermining patient trust at a vulnerable moment in their recovery.</p>'),
('10567', '2446', '_challenge', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_challenge'),
('10568', '2446', 'challenge_columns', '0'),
('10569', '2446', '_challenge_columns', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_challenge_columns'),
('10570', '2446', 'solution_title', 'Ninja Tropic\'s Approach: A Fusion of Science and Sensitivity'),
('10571', '2446', '_solution_title', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_solution_title'),
('10572', '2446', 'solution', '<p>Ninja Tropic developed a custom animation language built specifically for this project — soft watercolor-adjacent palettes, gentle motion, and abstract visual metaphors that gave complex neuroscientific concepts a warm, approachable quality. The visual style was deliberately non-clinical, avoiding the cold palette and sharp lines typical of medical animation.</p>
<p>The content was structured as a microlearning series, with each module covering a discrete aspect of the NDE experience: what happens physiologically during cardiac arrest, why the brain generates certain types of perceptions, and how these experiences are documented and understood within medical science. Narration was written with the patient — not the clinician — as the primary audience, using plain language validated for accessibility across educational levels.</p>'),
('10573', '2446', '_solution', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_solution'),
('10574', '2446', 'solution_columns', '0'),
('10575', '2446', '_solution_columns', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_solution_columns'),
