('11104', '2489', '_wp_attachment_metadata', 'a:6:{s:5:\"width\";i:1058;s:6:\"height\";i:583;s:4:\"file\";s:29:\"2026/06/solution-image-3.webp\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:357842;s:5:\"sizes\";a:4:{s:6:\"medium\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:29:\"solution-image-3-300x165.webp\";s:5:\"width\";i:300;s:6:\"height\";i:165;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/webp\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:43525;}s:5:\"large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:30:\"solution-image-3-1024x564.webp\";s:5:\"width\";i:1024;s:6:\"height\";i:564;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/webp\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:347442;}s:9:\"thumbnail\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:29:\"solution-image-3-150x150.webp\";s:5:\"width\";i:150;s:6:\"height\";i:150;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/webp\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:20354;}s:12:\"medium_large\";a:5:{s:4:\"file\";s:29:\"solution-image-3-768x423.webp\";s:5:\"width\";i:768;s:6:\"height\";i:423;s:9:\"mime-type\";s:10:\"image/webp\";s:8:\"filesize\";i:216454;}}s:10:\"image_meta\";a:12:{s:8:\"aperture\";s:1:\"0\";s:6:\"credit\";s:0:\"\";s:6:\"camera\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"caption\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"created_timestamp\";s:1:\"0\";s:9:\"copyright\";s:0:\"\";s:12:\"focal_length\";s:1:\"0\";s:3:\"iso\";s:1:\"0\";s:13:\"shutter_speed\";s:1:\"0\";s:5:\"title\";s:0:\"\";s:11:\"orientation\";s:1:\"0\";s:8:\"keywords\";a:0:{}}}'),
('11105', '2489', '_source_url', 'https://www.ninjatropic.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/04/TNC_M1-1-1.png'),
('11106', '2487', '_thumbnail_id', '2846'),
('11107', '2487', 'client_name', 'University of Delaware — DRCit! Initiative'),
('11108', '2487', '_client_name', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_client_name'),
('11109', '2487', 'client_intro', '<p>The University of Delaware\'s Disaster Research Center is a renowned institution providing insights into breaking news, developing events, and complex conditions leading to disaster. The DRCit! initiative offers scientifically informed guidance for practitioners, media outlets, and disaster science scholars.</p>'),
('11110', '2487', '_client_intro', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_client_intro'),
('11111', '2487', 'client_logo', ''),
('11112', '2487', '_client_logo', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_client_logo'),
('11113', '2487', 'challenge_title', 'Challenges Faced by DRCit! Before Working with Ninja Tropic'),
('11114', '2487', '_challenge_title', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_challenge_title'),
('11115', '2487', 'challenge', '<p>The DRCit! initiative faced a fundamental challenge in the field of disaster education: the target audience was not captive. Unlike corporate compliance training where completion is mandatory, DRCit!\'s learners — community practitioners, emergency managers, and the general public — had to choose to engage. Content that felt academic, preachy, or difficult to navigate would simply be abandoned.</p>
<p>Additionally, the subject matter required genuine depth. Disaster preparedness, mitigation, and response involve complex systems thinking that can\'t be reduced to a checklist — but the content had to be accessible enough to serve a broad public audience that included people with no formal emergency management background.</p>'),
('11116', '2487', '_challenge', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_challenge'),
('11117', '2487', 'challenge_columns', '0'),
('11118', '2487', '_challenge_columns', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_challenge_columns'),
('11119', '2487', 'solution_title', 'Ninja Tropic\'s Customized Interactive Video Approach'),
('11120', '2487', '_solution_title', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_solution_title'),
('11121', '2487', 'solution', '<p>Ninja Tropic conducted extensive learner research to understand the demographics, prior knowledge, and motivational drivers of DRCit!\'s target audience before developing a single frame of animation. This research directly shaped the instructional design: learning objectives were framed around practical decisions individuals face before and during disasters, rather than abstract principles.</p>
<p>The animated series featured a diverse cast of characters representing real community demographics, each navigating realistic disaster scenarios informed by actual case studies from the Disaster Research Center\'s institutional knowledge. 2D and 3D animation techniques were combined to create visual variety across the modules, with accessibility features including closed captions, screen-reader compatibility, and adjustable playback integrated throughout.</p>'),
('11122', '2487', '_solution', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_solution'),
('11123', '2487', 'solution_columns', '0'),
('11124', '2487', '_solution_columns', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_solution_columns'),
('11125', '2487', 'solution_image', '2489'),
('11126', '2487', '_solution_image', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_solution_image'),
('11127', '2487', 'solution_image_position', '0'),
('11128', '2487', '_solution_image_position', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_solution_image_position'),
('11129', '2487', 'results_title', 'Results of the Micro-Learning Video Series'),
('11130', '2487', '_results_title', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_results_title'),
('11131', '2487', 'results', '<ul>
 	<li><strong>High Voluntary Completion:</strong> Despite serving a non-captive audience, the series achieved completion rates that exceeded those of mandatory corporate training — validating the learner research investment and the engagement-first design approach.</li>
 	<li><strong>Knowledge Transfer:</strong> Pre- and post-module assessments demonstrated significant improvement in learner knowledge of disaster preparedness concepts, with retention rates higher than comparable text-based educational materials.</li>
 	<li><strong>Cross-Sector Adoption:</strong> The modules were adopted by emergency management agencies, community organizations, and academic institutions beyond DRCit!\'s initial target audience — a signal that the content quality exceeded expectations for publicly available educational resources.</li>
 	<li><strong>Media Recognition:</strong> The project received coverage in disaster research publications and was cited as a model for public-facing science communication in the emergency management field.</li>
</ul>'),
