('11242', '2498', 'client_name', 'CCRN Academy'),
('11243', '2498', '_client_name', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_client_name'),
('11244', '2498', 'client_intro', '<p>CCRN Academy is a leading provider of certification study guide training for the CCRN (Critical Care Registered Nurse) certification by the AACN (American Association of Critical-Care Nurses). Their mission is to help critical care nurses pass their certification exam with confidence.</p>'),
('11245', '2498', '_client_intro', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_client_intro'),
('11246', '2498', 'client_logo', '2500'),
('11247', '2498', '_client_logo', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_client_logo'),
('11248', '2498', 'challenge_title', 'The Problem with Traditional Certification Training'),
('11249', '2498', '_challenge_title', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_challenge_title'),
('11250', '2498', 'challenge', '<p>The CCRN certification is one of the most demanding credentialing exams in nursing — covering a vast body of clinical knowledge across critical care specialties with a pass rate that reflects its difficulty. Nurses preparing for the exam typically faced a market of substandard study resources: poorly recorded webinar-style reviews, dense textbooks with no interactivity, and practice question banks stripped of the clinical context that helps knowledge stick.</p>
<p>CCRN Academy saw an opportunity to fundamentally reimagine how nurses prepared for this exam — replacing passive content consumption with an active, microlearning-based study experience that matched how adult learners actually retain complex clinical information.</p>'),
('11251', '2498', '_challenge', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_challenge'),
('11252', '2498', 'challenge_columns', '0'),
('11253', '2498', '_challenge_columns', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_challenge_columns'),
('11254', '2498', 'solution_title', 'The Quest for a Dynamic Learning Solution'),
('11255', '2498', '_solution_title', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_solution_title'),
('11256', '2498', 'solution', '<p>Ninja Tropic collaborated with CCRN Academy\'s clinical subject matter experts to build a microlearning library covering every domain of the CCRN exam blueprint. Each module was designed as a standalone, five-to-seven-minute learning experience: a clinical scenario, a concept explanation, animated visuals reinforcing key pathophysiology or pharmacology, and a knowledge-check question before the learner moved on.</p>
<p>The production process involved multiple rounds of clinical review to ensure exam accuracy, with particular attention to the high-yield topics that carry the most weight on the actual certification exam. The final library was organized within an LMS that tracked progress, identified knowledge gaps, and guided learners toward the content most likely to improve their exam performance.</p>'),
('11257', '2498', '_solution', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_solution'),
('11258', '2498', 'solution_columns', '0'),
('11259', '2498', '_solution_columns', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_solution_columns'),
('11260', '2498', 'solution_image', '2501'),
('11261', '2498', '_solution_image', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_solution_image'),
('11262', '2498', 'solution_image_position', '0'),
('11263', '2498', '_solution_image_position', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_solution_image_position'),
('11264', '2498', 'results_title', 'Go-to-Market Strategy and Results'),
('11265', '2498', '_results_title', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_results_title'),
('11266', '2498', 'results', '<ul>
<li><strong>98% Pass Rate:</strong> CCRN Academy\'s learners achieved a 98% first-attempt pass rate — a benchmark that positioned the program as the most effective CCRN study resource available and became the centerpiece of every marketing claim.</li>
<li><strong>500% Annual ROI:</strong> The combination of high pass rates, word-of-mouth growth from satisfied nurses, and efficient content delivery generated a 500% annual return on the initial production investment.</li>
<li><strong>Category Leadership:</strong> The production quality and clinical accuracy of the Ninja Tropic-produced content established CCRN Academy as the premium study resource in a category previously dominated by low-production alternatives.</li>
<li><strong>Nurse Community Adoption:</strong> Critical care nurses began sharing the academy through professional networks and social media, creating organic growth driven by peer recommendations — the most credible marketing channel in a clinical professional community.</li></ul>'),
('11267', '2498', '_results', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_results'),
('11268', '2498', 'results_columns', '1'),
('11269', '2498', '_results_columns', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_results_columns'),
('11270', '2498', 'linked_project', '2267'),
('11271', '2498', '_linked_project', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_linked_project'),
('11272', '2498', 'project_section_title', 'See It In Action'),
('11273', '2498', '_project_section_title', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_project_section_title'),
('11274', '2498', 'project_section_text', ''),
('11275', '2498', '_project_section_text', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_project_section_text'),
('11276', '2487', '_edit_lock', '1782318173:1'),
('11277', '2487', 'rank_math_seo_score', '57'),
('11278', '2487', 'rank_math_contentai_score', 'a:5:{s:8:\"keywords\";s:5:\"74.51\";s:9:\"wordCount\";s:1:\"0\";s:9:\"linkCount\";s:1:\"0\";s:12:\"headingCount\";s:1:\"0\";s:10:\"mediaCount\";s:1:\"0\";}'),
('11279', '2487', '_edit_last', '1'),
('11280', '2502', 'client_name', 'University of Delaware — DRCit! Initiative'),
('11281', '2502', '_client_name', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_client_name'),
('11282', '2502', 'client_intro', '<p>The University of Delaware\'s Disaster Research Center is a renowned institution providing insights into breaking news, developing events, and complex conditions leading to disaster. The DRCit! initiative offers scientifically informed guidance for practitioners, media outlets, and disaster science scholars.</p>'),
('11283', '2502', '_client_intro', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_client_intro'),
('11284', '2502', 'client_logo', ''),
('11285', '2502', '_client_logo', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_client_logo'),
('11286', '2502', 'challenge_title', 'Challenges Faced by DRCit! Before Working with Ninja Tropic'),
('11287', '2502', '_challenge_title', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_challenge_title'),
('11288', '2502', 'challenge', '<p>The DRCit! initiative faced a fundamental challenge in the field of disaster education: the target audience was not captive. Unlike corporate compliance training where completion is mandatory, DRCit!\'s learners — community practitioners, emergency managers, and the general public — had to choose to engage. Content that felt academic, preachy, or difficult to navigate would simply be abandoned.</p>
<p>Additionally, the subject matter required genuine depth. Disaster preparedness, mitigation, and response involve complex systems thinking that can\'t be reduced to a checklist — but the content had to be accessible enough to serve a broad public audience that included people with no formal emergency management background.</p>'),
('11289', '2502', '_challenge', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_challenge'),
('11290', '2502', 'challenge_columns', '0'),
('11291', '2502', '_challenge_columns', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_challenge_columns'),
('11292', '2502', 'solution_title', 'Ninja Tropic\'s Customized Interactive Video Approach'),
('11293', '2502', '_solution_title', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_solution_title'),
('11294', '2502', 'solution', '<p>Ninja Tropic conducted extensive learner research to understand the demographics, prior knowledge, and motivational drivers of DRCit!\'s target audience before developing a single frame of animation. This research directly shaped the instructional design: learning objectives were framed around practical decisions individuals face before and during disasters, rather than abstract principles.</p>
<p>The animated series featured a diverse cast of characters representing real community demographics, each navigating realistic disaster scenarios informed by actual case studies from the Disaster Research Center\'s institutional knowledge. 2D and 3D animation techniques were combined to create visual variety across the modules, with accessibility features including closed captions, screen-reader compatibility, and adjustable playback integrated throughout.</p>'),
('11295', '2502', '_solution', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_solution'),
('11296', '2502', 'solution_columns', '0'),
('11297', '2502', '_solution_columns', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_solution_columns'),
('11298', '2502', 'solution_image', '2489'),
('11299', '2502', '_solution_image', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_solution_image'),
('11300', '2502', 'solution_image_position', '0'),
('11301', '2502', '_solution_image_position', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_solution_image_position'),
('11302', '2502', 'results_title', 'Results of the Micro-Learning Video Series'),
('11303', '2502', '_results_title', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_results_title'),
('11304', '2502', 'results', '<ul>
 	<li><strong>High Voluntary Completion:</strong> Despite serving a non-captive audience, the series achieved completion rates that exceeded those of mandatory corporate training — validating the learner research investment and the engagement-first design approach.</li>
 	<li><strong>Knowledge Transfer:</strong> Pre- and post-module assessments demonstrated significant improvement in learner knowledge of disaster preparedness concepts, with retention rates higher than comparable text-based educational materials.</li>
 	<li><strong>Cross-Sector Adoption:</strong> The modules were adopted by emergency management agencies, community organizations, and academic institutions beyond DRCit!\'s initial target audience — a signal that the content quality exceeded expectations for publicly available educational resources.</li>
 	<li><strong>Media Recognition:</strong> The project received coverage in disaster research publications and was cited as a model for public-facing science communication in the emergency management field.</li>
</ul>'),
('11305', '2502', '_results', 'field_ninjatheme_cs_results'),
