<!-- wp:column {\"verticalAlignment\":\"center\"} -->
<div class=\"wp-block-column is-vertically-aligned-center\"><!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Frequently Asked Question, <em>Answered</em></strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:separator {\"className\":\"is-style-dots\",\"backgroundColor\":\"luminous-vivid-orange\"} -->
<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-text-color has-luminous-vivid-orange-color has-alpha-channel-opacity has-luminous-vivid-orange-background-color has-background is-style-dots\"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>How Much Does It Cost to Create eLearning?</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The cost of eLearning development depends on various factors, including the complexity of the project, the desired production value, and the specific features and functionalities you require. We pride ourselves on being industry leaders in terms of cost-effectiveness due to our specialization in eLearning, our strategic use of AI technologies, and our efficient team structure.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Our courses typically range from $5,000 to $50,000 for an hour of content. However, it’s important to note that these are estimates, and the final cost will depend on your specific needs and requirements. We’ll work closely with you to understand your budget and create a solution that aligns with your goals and financial constraints.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>How Long Does It Take to Develop a Custom eLearning Course?</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Timelines for eLearning development can vary depending on the complexity of the project, but we typically estimate anywhere from 7 weeks to 4 months. It depends on factors like the amount of content, the level of interactivity, and the need for custom features. We’ll provide you with a detailed timeline at the beginning of the project.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>
<!-- /wp:column --></div>
<!-- /wp:columns -->

