<!-- wp:column {\"width\":\"66.66%\"} -->
<div class=\"wp-block-column\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\"><!-- wp:heading {\"textAlign\":\"center\",\"level\":1} -->
<h1 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center\">Kinetic Typography</h1>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:separator {\"className\":\"is-style-dots\",\"backgroundColor\":\"luminous-vivid-orange\"} -->
<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-text-color has-luminous-vivid-orange-color has-alpha-channel-opacity has-luminous-vivid-orange-background-color has-background is-style-dots\"/>
<!-- /wp:separator -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>(Motion-Lettering) is a graphic animation technique that utilizes moving text and icons to create engaging visual content. It is a popular style for eLearning as it enhances the effectiveness of the learning experience by promoting engagement, aiding in memory retention, and improving comprehension. Kinetic typography can be used to emphasize important points, demonstrate concepts, and make information more digestible for learners. Paired with an eLearning design that aligns with learners, it can help to make learning more interesting, interactive, and effective.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

