<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)</h2>
<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why are Subject Matter Expert (SME) interviews so important for training?</h3>
SMEs possess the critical, specialized “source code” for your content. Conducting structured interviews with them ensures that your training programs capture the explicit procedures and implicit wisdom necessary for learners to succeed, rather than relying on generic information.
<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What is the “Curse of Knowledge” in an SME interview?</h3>
The “Curse of Knowledge” occurs when an expert is so deeply knowledgeable that they forget what it’s like to be a beginner. During an interview, they might unconsciously skip foundational steps or use heavy industry jargon, which is why an instructional designer must guide the conversation to clarify those blind spots.
<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How should I prepare for a Subject Matter Expert interview?</h3>
Never walk into an interview cold. You should always research the topic, review existing documentation, and understand industry terminology beforehand. Additionally, schedule a 30-minute kick-off meeting to define the goals, audience, and clear performance objectives before the actual knowledge transfer session begins.', 'Subject Matter Expert Interview Guide: Complete Template & Best Practices for L&D Success', 'Custom eLearning content development made simple—learn how to create engaging, results-driven training with expert tips, examples, and best practices', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'subject-matter-expert-interview', '', '', '2026-06-29 00:21:37', '2026-06-29 00:21:37', '', '0', 'http://localhost:8080/subject-matter-expert-interview/', '0', 'post', '', '0'),
