('2579', '7', '2024-01-10 21:01:22', '2024-01-11 04:01:22', '<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>The Comprehensive LMS Implementation Project Plan for Modern Learning (2024)</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The importance of Learning Management Systems (LMS) in fostering modern learning experiences cannot be overstated. LMS implementation has become a crucial step for organizations seeking to enhance their learning and development strategies in alignment with digital trends.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/lms-calculator/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Optimizing Talent LMS for HR and L&D: Intuitive LMS Calculator</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/lms-administration-pricing/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Unlock Your LMS Potential with Our Exclusive Plans</strong></a><a href=\"#title5\"></a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This comprehensive project plan delves into the essentials of <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/lms-consultants/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LMS</a> implementation, offering insights and strategies to ensure a successful transition to digital learning. Whether you\'re an educational institution or a corporate entity, understanding the nuances of LMS implementation can significantly impact your approach to training and development in the digital age.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} -->
<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The Strategic LMS Implementation Plan</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A well-planned LMS implementation can streamline learning processes, enhance employee training, and ultimately contribute to organizational success. By following these strategic steps and incorporating best practices, organizations can lay the groundwork for a successful and impactful learning platform.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>1. Assessing Organizational Needs: Understanding Your Learning Objectives and Requirements</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The first step in LMS implementation is a thorough evaluation of your organization’s learning needs. This process involves identifying skills gaps, training objectives, and the specific requirements of different learner groups within your organization.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Consider conducting a comprehensive needs analysis to understand the various dimensions of your training requirements, including technical skills, compliance training, and professional development. This evaluation will provide valuable insights into the type of content, learning methodologies, and technological features your LMS should support.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>2. Establishing Clear Learning Goals</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Set clear, measurable learning goals aligned with your organizational objectives. These goals should guide the selection of LMS features and functionalities, ensuring that the platform you choose can effectively support your training initiatives. Consider both short-term training needs and long-term educational goals to ensure the sustainability and scalability of your LMS.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>3. Choosing the Right LMS: Identifying Key Features and Functionalities</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Selecting the appropriate LMS is a decision that significantly impacts the effectiveness of your learning initiatives. Key criteria to consider include the <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/lms-management-services-the-challenge-of-filling-the-lms-role/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LMS’s features</a>, scalability, user-friendliness, and integration capabilities. Look for an LMS that offers a robust set of tools and features such as course authoring, gamification, mobile accessibility, and advanced analytics. Ensure that the platform is scalable and can grow with your organization’s evolving needs.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>4. Ensuring Seamless Integration and Compatibility</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The LMS should seamlessly integrate with your existing systems, such as Human Resources Information Systems (HRIS), Customer Relationship Management (CRM) platforms, and other enterprise software. This integration is crucial for data consistency, streamlined workflows, and a cohesive learning experience. Additionally, assess the LMS’s compatibility with various content formats and eLearning standards to ensure a smooth transition and content migration.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>5. Building a Project Team</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Assembling a Cross-Functional Team for LMS Implementation A successful LMS implementation requires the formation of a skilled, cross-functional project team. This team should include IT specialists, training and development professionals, content creators, and representatives from the user community. Each member brings unique insights and expertise, contributing to a well-rounded implementation strategy.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>6. Defining Roles and Responsibilities</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Clearly define the roles and responsibilities of each team member. This clarity will facilitate effective collaboration and ensure that all aspects of the LMS implementation, from technical setup to content development and user training, are adequately addressed. Encourage open communication and regular meetings to keep the team aligned and on track toward implementation goals.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Implementing an LMS is a strategic process that requires careful planning and consideration. By thoroughly assessing organizational needs, choosing an LMS that aligns with your learning objectives, and building a competent project team, organizations can lay a solid foundation for a successful LMS rollout. These steps are instrumental in creating a dynamic and effective learning environment that supports organizational growth and employee development.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Executing the Project Plan: LMS Implementation: Setting Up, Training, and Testing for Success</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>LMS implementation hinges on detailed planning, careful configuration, comprehensive user training, and robust testing protocols. Now that we are done with planning, let\'s discuss a step-by-step guide on setting up your LMS, delivering essential training to different user groups, and conducting thorough testing to gather feedback for continuous improvement.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>7. Setting Up the LMS: Configuring and Customizing Your Learning Platform</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The first step in LMS implementation is setting up and configuring the platform. This process involves several critical stages:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li><strong>System Configuration:</strong> Begin with the basic setup of the LMS, which includes configuring server settings, user roles, and security parameters. Ensure that the system settings align with your organization’s IT policies and learning objectives.</li>
<li><strong>Customizing the Interface:</strong> Customize the LMS interface to reflect your organization\'s brand and learning culture. This customization can include logo incorporation, color scheme adjustments, and layout modifications to enhance user experience and engagement.</li>
<li><strong>Course Setup:</strong> Upload and organize your learning content. Set up course structures, upload materials, and define learning paths. Ensure that the course designs align with your overall training objectives and cater to diverse learning styles.</li>
<li><strong>Integrations:</strong> Integrate the LMS with other critical systems like HRIS, CRM, or talent management systems for streamlined data flow and cohesive functionality.</li>
<li><strong>User Training and Support:</strong> Empowering Administrators, Instructors, and Learners. Effective training and support are crucial for maximizing the benefits of your new LMS.</li>
<li><strong>Administrator Training:</strong> Train your LMS administrators on system management, user support, and data analytics. This training ensures that they are well-equipped to manage the LMS, troubleshoot issues, and generate insightful reports.</li>
<li><strong>Instructor Training:</strong> Instructors should receive comprehensive training on creating and managing course content, engaging with learners, and tracking progress. This training will enable them to utilize the LMS effectively for delivering impactful learning experiences.</li>
<li><strong>Learner Orientation:</strong> Provide learners with orientation sessions to familiarize them with navigating the LMS, accessing courses, and utilizing available resources. This orientation is critical for encouraging active engagement and ensuring that learners can leverage the full.</li>
<li><strong>Testing and Feedback:</strong> Ensuring a Flawless LMS Experience Through Pilot Testing.</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Before a full-scale rollout, it’s imperative to conduct pilot testing</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Projecting Plan: LMS Implementation Pilot Testing</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This phase allows you to test the functionality of the LMS in a controlled environment, identify any technical glitches, and assess the overall user experience.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>8. Gathering Feedback</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Collect feedback from the pilot test participants. This feedback is invaluable for identifying areas of improvement, understanding user preferences, and making necessary adjustments before broader deployment.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>9. Iterative Improvements</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Use the feedback to make iterative improvements to the LMS setup, content, and training modules. Continuous refinement based on user input is key to achieving an optimal learning environment. Implementing an LMS is a multifaceted process that requires meticulous planning, execution, and continuous refinement.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>LMS Tracking and Reporting: How to use LMS analytics to track learner progress, engagement, and course effectiveness.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The journey doesn’t end with implementation. The real challenge lies in effectively monitoring and evaluating the LMS\'s performance. Let’s discuss some insights into leveraging LMS analytics for tracking and reporting, as well as strategies for ensuring continuous improvement of your LMS.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>10. Tracking Learner Progress</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Use the LMS’s tracking capabilities to monitor individual learner progress. This includes course completion rates, assessment scores, and time spent on each module. Tracking progress helps in identifying learners who might need additional support and recognizing those who excel.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>11. Measuring Engagement</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Engagement metrics such as log-in frequency, discussion participation, and interactive content usage offer insights into how engaging the learning content is. These metrics are vital for understanding the effectiveness of your courses and identifying areas that might require more interactive or compelling content.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>12. Evaluating Course Effectiveness</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Analyze course completion and assessment data to evaluate the effectiveness of your training programs. High completion rates and positive assessment outcomes typically indicate that the course content is relevant and well-received by learners.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>13. Continuous Improvement: Adapting Based on Performance Data</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Effective monitoring and continuous improvement of your LMS are vital to its success as a learning tool. By leveraging LMS analytics for insightful tracking and reporting and adopting a data-driven approach to content and functionality updates, organizations can ensure their LMS remains a dynamic and effective platform. This commitment to ongoing evaluation and enhancement is crucial in fostering an engaging, responsive, and results-oriented learning environment.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} -->
<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">\">Final Thoughts: LMS Implementation Project Plan</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>An LMS is more than just a digital platform; it\'s a catalyst for educational transformation and corporate training efficiency. In the heart of digital learning, an LMS provides a centralized, interactive, and accessible platform for delivering, tracking, and managing training programs. It\'s a tool that adapts to the evolving needs of modern learners, enabling organizations to create, deliver, and monitor training anywhere, anytime.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The LMS should be a dynamic platform, evolving with the changing needs of your organization. Regularly review and update the content, and stay abreast of new features or updates to the LMS software. Encourage ongoing feedback from users to continually refine and improve the learning experience. In embracing these principles, organizations can harness the full potential of an LMS for sustained educational and training excellence.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>At Ninja Tropic, we specialize in crafting dynamic and tailored LMS solutions that align with the ever-evolving needs of modern learners. Let us be your partner in creating a centralized, interactive, and accessible platform for delivering, tracking, and managing training programs. <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/elearning-video-animation-companies-free-consultation/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Contact us today to kickstart the development of an LMS </a>that will empower your learners to thrive in the digital age.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'The Comprehensive LMS Implementation Project Plan for Modern Learning (2024)', 'Unlock the potential of modern learning with our Comprehensive LMS Implementation Project Plan. Elevate education and training in 2024. Explore now!', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'lms-implementation-project-plan', '', '', '2026-06-25 20:25:55', '2026-06-25 20:25:55', '', '0', 'http://localhost:8080/lms-implementation-project-plan/', '0', 'post', '', '0'),
('2580', '0', '2026-06-05 22:54:01', '2026-06-05 22:54:01', 'LMS Implementation Project Plan. From: The Comprehensive LMS Implementation Project Plan for Modern Learning (2024).', 'LMS Implementation Project Plan', 'LMS Implementation Project Plan', 'inherit', 'open', 'closed', '', 'lms-implementation-project-plan-2', '', '', '2026-06-05 22:54:01', '2026-06-05 22:54:01', '', '2579', 'http://localhost:8080/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/Beyond-Cost-1.webp', '0', 'attachment', 'image/webp', '0'),
('2581', '7', '2023-09-28 13:10:05', '2023-09-28 20:10:05', '<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":1} -->
<h1>Top 16 Training Video Production Companies (2023)</h1>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In a survey that included 2,000+ companies, <a href=\"https://research.com/education/video-training-statistics\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">74%</a> of trainers said that they use video learning as part of their training. If that says something, it’s that video production is at the core of modern training strategies.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>With that being that case, it pays to invest in quality video production – otherwise, you run the risk of producing low-quality, ineffective videos that don’t match up with your training objectives.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title1\">B2B Training Done Right: 7 Essential Components Every Quality Corporate Training Video Production Company Must Have</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title2\">Top 16 Training Video Production Companies in 2023</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title3\">Need a Video Production Company for Your Training Videos?</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>On top of that, you\'ll get the snores when it comes to engagement. It\'s a lose-lose situation.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>But with thousands of video production companies out there, choosing the right one for your training program is no walk in the park. That\'s why we\'ve put together this list of 16 top-tier training video production companies to help you narrow down your options and find the best fit for your next project.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} -->
<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">B2B Training Done Right: 7 Essential Components Every Quality Corporate Training Video Production Company Must Have</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>To be able to choose the right training video production company, you need to first know what to look for, right? Below is your 7-point checklist to know you\'re in the right hands.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>1. Expertise</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It goes without saying that the company you choose should have expertise in corporate training videos. They\'re different in terms of objectives and content, so you want to be sure that the company you\'re looking at understands the nuances of training videos.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>What\'s more, if possible, you should look for a company that has experience in your specific industry. For instance, if you need retail training videos, safety training videos, or something similar, the more they know the subject matter inside-out, the better.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>2. Cost-Effectiveness</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Corporate training videos can get expensive. To save costs, look for a video production company that has the tools and resources to complete your project without breaking the bank. It\'s also important to make sure you have clarity on what\'s included in their services – from pre-production planning to post-production editing. Aim for the highest value for your money.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>3. Client Experience</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>References and <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/customer-testimonials/\">testimonials</a> are your best friends when it comes to choosing the right video production company. A good track record tells you that they provide a great client experience, so don\'t hesitate to ask for direct feedback from previous clients and take your time to read through reviews.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>4. Communication</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It\'s crucial to have an understanding of how the company works and what its process looks like. Do they clearly discuss timelines, deliverables, costs, etc.? Do they provide you with updates during the process? It’s also important to find out if they’ll be open and responsive to any feedback you might have during the project.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>\">\">5. Video Portfolio & Reviews</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>\">\">It\'s easy to go on and on about how great certain training video production companies are, but the proof of their excellence lies in the quality of their work. Ask to see some of their previous work – if they have a <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/elearning-video-portfolio/\">portfolio</a>, even better! And again, look for reviews from industry professionals and former clients to make sure you\'re not signing up for sub-par quality.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>6. Custom-Tailored Services</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>No two corporate videos are the same, so you\'ll want to make sure that your video production company can provide custom-tailored services.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Ask them if they\'d be willing to put together a package specifically designed for your project, or if they have any suggestions for how to best address your needs. One-size-fits-all solutions rarely work, so you\'ll want to make sure your production company is willing to meet your specific requirements.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>7. Turnaround Time</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Lastly, make sure to ask about turnaround time. If you have a tight deadline, then it\'s all the more important that your chosen video production company can deliver in a timely manner. On top of that, find out if they provide any revisions and determine how long those might take so you don\'t run the risk of missing your deadline.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Now that your checklist is complete, it\'s time to turn your attention to finding the best video production companies for corporate videos. Here are our top picks, and it\'s your call to decide which one is right for your project needs.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>1. Ninja Tropic – Best Overall Training Video Production Company</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>At <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/\">Ninja Tropic</a>, we really get it when it comes to e-learning video production. Our promise is to make the \"click next\" learning modules a thing of the past for your training videos by following our science-backed training video production process that focuses on improving retention and changing behavior.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>For our training video production services, we use creative storytelling, motion graphics, animations, simulators – just about anything to make sure we produce training videos that are interesting and engaging. Plus, we have a proven track record of helping companies create training videos that <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/case-studies/\">make an impact</a>, so you can rest assured that your project is in experienced hands. That\'s all while staying true to your brand!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Founded In:</strong> 2016<br /><strong>Known For:</strong> Animation & microlearning training videosTeam <br /><strong>Members:</strong> 1-10<br /><strong>Client Praise:</strong> \"They are very fast and efficient. They also had a great process to show our SMEs which simplified everything. What I appreciate is the fact that they took the time to learn our goals. We needed content that was engaging and effective for our sales staff and they got it! – Raquel C.\"</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>2. Studio B Films</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>From visually captivating graphics to poignant storytelling, <strong>Studio B Film</strong>s is a corporate training video production company that offers the perfect blend of art and science. What you\'ll love about them is how hands-on they are with each project, working closely with you to find out the right approach that will keep employees engaged. To top it off, their years of experience provide them with that extra edge when it comes to creating training videos that are both entertaining and effective.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Founded In:</strong> 1992<br /><strong>Known For:</strong> Training video production<br /><strong>Members:</strong> 10-49<br /><strong>Client Praise:</strong> \"You can tell everyone who works at Studio B cares about doing a job right, and that is worth every penny. – Kathryn Quigley, Senior Producer, Lawrence Hall of Science\"</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>WyzOwl</strong> is the perfect corporate training video production company when you want to get a lot of bang for your buck without compromising on quality. And with their efficient work process, they can handle large-scale projects with ease so you don\'t have to worry about tight deadlines or unexpected delays. Plus, handling feedback with finesse is also one of their strong suits – allowing you to have maximum control over the outcome of your video.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Founded In:</strong> 2009<br /><strong>Known For:</strong> All-in-one animated video production<br /><strong>Members:</strong> 10-49<br /><strong>Client Praise:</strong>\"It was such a pleasure to work with Wyzowl! During every stage of the project, they delivered amazing work that required very little revisions – saving time for the both of us! Thank you for making my life a little easier. I am so happy with my custom video and would most definitely recommend Wyzowl! – Kelsey Berry, Qspex\"</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>4. Demo Duck</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Taking complex topics and making them easier to understand – that\'s what Demo Duck does best. As a corporate training video production company, they specialize in animation and motion graphics to explain intricate systems and concepts in a way that\'s both fun and engaging. And with clients like Dropbox, American Express, and the American Cancer Society under their belt, you can trust your project will be in good hands.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Founded In:</strong> 2011<br /><strong>Known For:</strong> Animated training videos<br /><strong>Members:</strong> 10-49<br /><strong>Client Praise:</strong> \"Demo Duck’s animations are educational, but they never sacrifice the brand’s fun, youthful essence. Their effective and enchanting videos are a direct result of their commitment to using their artistry to accomplish business goals. Beyond their creative talents, they are delightful to work with. – Liza Heiligman, Marketing Director, Wheels for Wishes\"</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>\">\">5. Mind Spring</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Mind Spring</strong> is a video production company with innovation at its core. They understand the importance of understanding your business objectives and how best to incorporate them into video content that will engage, educate, and motivate learners. The result is a blend of innovation, creativity, and storytelling that keeps learners coming back for more.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Founded In:</strong> 2011<br /><strong>Known For:</strong> Creative training videos using immersive technology<br /><strong>Members:</strong> 51-100<br /><strong>Client Praise:</strong> \"They were able to lead us through the process and helped us create something we could never do on our own. We weren\'t entirely sure what to expect, however, they were able to quickly understand what we were looking to achieve, and had a flawless process to achieve it.\"</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>6. Second Home Studios</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Second Home Studios</strong> is a corporate training video company that specializes in animation. That means they can take topics you\'d never think could be exciting and turn them into visually stunning masterpieces. With a track record of successful projects across different industries, they can handle any training video project you throw their way and will make sure you get the results you expect (if not better!)</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Founded In:</strong> 2004<br /><strong>Known For:</strong> Animated video production<br /><strong>Members:</strong> 1-10<br /><strong>Client Praise:</strong> \"These guys are storytellers. They helped us articulate Rekorderlig\'s complete life history in a succinct and stylish way. The team at Second Home is responsive, adaptable, and above all, they care. What\'s not to like? – Gareth Whittle, MD, Chilli Marketing\"</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>7. Content Beta</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Specializing in tech and B2B video production, <strong>Content Beta</strong> is a reliable choice if you\'re looking for fast results. They handle every project with skillful precision, all while maintaining a cost-effective approach that will work for your budget. With their expertise, you can be sure that your video won\'t experience any unexpected hiccups and will come out exactly as you imagined it.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>8. Explainify</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Explainify</strong> is a video production company that specializes in animated video production. Apart from creating can\'t-miss explainer videos and demo videos, they also excel in making your experience entirely stress-free through a process they call – you guessed it – Frustration-Free process. Guiding you through the five steps of uncovery, scripting, storyboarding, vocal talent, animation, and sound design – they make sure you get the perfect video tailored to your needs.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Founded In:</strong> 2012<br /><strong>Known For:</strong> Animated training videos<br /><strong>Members:</strong> 10-49<br /><strong>Client Praise:</strong> \"The end video was amazing, but what blew me away was how easy it was to get to that end product with their team. – Jake Jorgovan, Founder, Lead Cookie\"</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>9. Whatastory</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Just from their brand name, you can already tell that <strong>Whatastory</strong> is all about telling stories using explainer videos. They\'re a full-service production company that puts an emphasis on crafting compelling stories that engage audiences from start to finish. Whether it\'s for training, marketing, or promotional purposes, they have the skills and know-how to create a stunning video that will keep viewers hooked from beginning to end.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Founded In:</strong> 2015<br /><strong>Known For:</strong> Explainer training videos<br /><strong>Members:</strong> 10-49<br /><strong>Client Praise:</strong> \"They are responsive, sincere, and passionate about their clients\' work and effective in achieving their vision. – Clev Wong, Principal Tech Consultant, CTARe\"</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>10. Testimonial Hero</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Capturing a customer\'s or even an employee\'s story in the form of a video is an effective way to gain customers\' trust and loyalty. <strong>Testimonial Her</strong>o specializes in producing powerful videos that capture the true essence of each customer\'s experience. From scripting and shooting all the way to editing, their team will work with you throughout every stage of the production process to ensure that each video showcases your customer\'s story in the most impactful way possible.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Founded In:</strong> 2017<br /><strong>Known For:</strong> Customer and employee testimonial videos<br /><strong>Members:</strong> 11-50<br /><strong>Client Praise:</strong> \"They produced high-quality testimonials remotely and treated our clients as if they were their own. – Graham Eichman, Director of Business Development, Singlemind\"</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>11. Digital Spark Studios</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Digital Spark Studios</strong> is a full-service video production company with an expansive portfolio that includes giants like P&G, Lexus, Atrium Health, Food Lion, and beyond. Their ability to tailor their processes to any industry makes them a great choice for any video project, so you can count on them for a consistent delivery across multiple industries. They excel in motion graphics, so if you want to add an extra touch of creativity to your videos, they\'re certainly your go-to.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Founded In:</strong> 2014<br /><strong>Known For:</strong> High-quality training videos<br /><strong>Members:</strong> 2-9<br /><strong>Client Praise:</strong> \"They are quick to identify a solution and work to create an amazing shot.- Manager, InVue\"</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>12. Next Thought Studios</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Affordable, memorable, and fun – that\'s what <strong>Next Thought Studios</strong> stands for. They specialize in producing videos that leave a lasting impression on viewers and help them understand complex concepts quickly. With this team of experienced video professionals, you can trust that your project will be executed properly from start to finish.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Founded In:</strong> 2011<br /><strong>Known For:</strong> Affordable corporate training video production<br /><strong>Members:</strong> 10-49<br /><strong>Client Praise:</strong> \"I\'d describe them as generally laid back and easygoing, but they\'re always on top of everything. – Chris Kramer, Partner, House of Kaizen\"</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>13. Pigeon Studio</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>With a reputation for excellence, <strong>Pigeon Studio</strong> is one of the top video production companies around. Their ability to take complex ideas and turn them into simple, effective animated video visuals makes them a great choice for any project. They’re passionate about storytelling and have a knack for creating emotionally engaging videos that capture viewers\' attention from start to finish.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Founded In:</strong> 2012<br /><strong>Known For:</strong> Animated training video production<br /><strong>Members:</strong> 10-49<br /><strong>Client Praise:</strong> \"It was a true partnership and a creative exchange relationship.- Agnieszka Koterba, Senior Producer, Ars Thanea SA\"</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>14. Slow Clap Productions</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Slack, GitHub, eBay, Adobe, Playstation – these aren\'t just big names, they\'re some of the many clients that <strong>Slow Clap Productions</strong> has served. This team of professionals takes pride in their work and puts an emphasis on delivering a top-notch service every single time. If you\'re looking for a production company that can handle everything from concept to delivery, then Slow Clap Productions is the perfect choice.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Founded In:</strong> 2014<br /><strong>Known For:</strong> High-quality video production services<br /><strong>Members:</strong> 2-9<br /><strong>Client Praise:</strong> “They can tackle a large variety of projects, from small to large ones, and they’re always very fun to work with. – Nick Goldman, Producer, Trademark”</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>15. Blue Carrot</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Blue Carrot</strong> is a corporate video production company that knows all the ins and outs of the e-learning arena. For you, that means you can count on them to create any type of video you need, from training and explainers to onboarding and promo videos. Plus, the fact that this instructional video production company can serve you from pre-production to post-production means you won\'t have to worry about managing multiple companies in order to get the job done.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Founded In:</strong> 2014<br /><strong>Known For:</strong> Full-cycle video production for marketing and e-learning<br /><strong>Members:</strong> 2-9<br /><strong>Client Praise:</strong> \"Their customer service is above and beyond anything else we came across on the market.- Alistair Cousins, Marketing Manager, TrouDigital\"</p>
