('2586', '0', '2026-06-05 22:54:05', '2026-06-05 22:54:05', 'eLearning Interactivity. From: eLearning Interactivity 2023: The 4 Levels & How to Use Them (Plus Benefits).', 'eLearning Interactivity', 'eLearning Interactivity', 'inherit', 'open', 'closed', '', 'elearning-interactivity', '', '', '2026-06-05 22:54:05', '2026-06-05 22:54:05', '', '2585', 'http://localhost:8080/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/elearning-interactivity.webp', '0', 'attachment', 'image/webp', '0'),
('2587', '7', '2023-07-20 11:07:42', '2023-07-20 18:07:42', '<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":1} -->
<h1>New Hire Time to Productivity: How to Improve Employee Performance</h1>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>After organizations spend months-on-end in the hiring process, searching for the right candidate, right on the new hire\'s first day, they already have one question in mind:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>\"When will I start to see results?\"</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title1\">What Is New Hire Time to Productivity?</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title2\">How Can New Hire Time to Productivity Be Tracked?</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title3\">Why Track New Hires Time to Productivity?</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title4\">How Long Until Employees Are Fully Productive?</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title5\">Time to Productivity Contributing Factors</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title6\">Final Thoughts: New Hire Time to Productivity</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Performance expectations are high, and there\'s often pressure to get newly-hired employees up and running as soon as possible. Understandably, today\'s world of ever-increasing competition and shrinking margins has put greater emphasis on the need to maximize performance from day one.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>But without proper employee productivity metrics to track performance, evaluations are often subjective (mostly a pure guessing game!), and managers can’t always identify which new hire onboarding strategies are working best.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>That\'s where measuring new hire time to productivity comes in. Here\'s what you need to know about it.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>New hire time to productivity is a measurement of how long it takes for an employee to go from onboarding to being fully productive and meeting performance goals. In other words, it\'s the time a new employee takes to start adding value to the company from the day they start working.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This metric is used to measure the effectiveness of onboarding strategies, and it can help managers have an objective view of how well their new-hire training and onboarding strategies are performing. That\'s because supporting new employees from the get-go helps them become productive faster, and in turn, reduces time to productivity.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When it comes to how to measure time to productivity, there are a number of methods that organizations can use. However, the most common one is by subtracting the employee\'s start date from the date they become fully productive.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Similarly, to get the total average time of new hire time to productivity, organizations can track multiple employees at once by adding the total number of days for all new hires to reach full productivity over a given time frame and dividing it by the total number of new hires.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>For this to work, managers should create performance goals for new hires that must be met in a certain period of time- usually within the first few weeks or months of employment (<a href=\"https://seismic.com/blog/employee-onboarding-software-15-employee-engagement-stats/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">60% of companies</a> don\'t bother setting milestones or goals for new hires, so this is crucial.)</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This could range from completing specific certifications or <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/blog-how-to-plan-create-effective-employee-training-videos-step-by-step-guide/\">training videos</a> to reaching certain role-related performance targets, such as hitting a certain sales target or reaching a customer satisfaction score.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Then, measure how long it took them to reach those goals and calculate their time to productivity.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This metric can then be used to compare new hires and see how their onboarding experience is impacting their productivity. This can also be used to spot any areas of improvement and help HR leaders tweak their onboarding programs accordingly to maximize efficiency.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Pro Tip: To unify the calculation of time to productivity, it helps if the organization has a very clear definition of what “full productivity” means. This will provide everyone with an understanding of the expected goals and performance standards for new hires, making it easier to track their time to productivity and measure overall success.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Using the new hire productivity metric isn\'t only used to evaluate whether new employees are becoming productive or not. It can also be used to inform various HR decisions, providing insights into the following.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Onboarding Process Efficiency</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The general rule is that the faster a new hire becomes productive, the more effective the onboarding process is. Tracking time to productivity can help organizations determine if their current onboarding program is efficient or not. Most times, the \"standard\" onboarding process ends up hindering new employees from becoming productive faster.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Company Health</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Onboarding isn\'t the only factor that affects the time to productivity. If an organization is confident in its onboarding program yet it\'s still experiencing long times to productivity, it could be an indication of deeper issues within the organization.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Such issues could include unclear goals or a broken culture – all of which can affect new employees just as much as onboarding. As such, this could give a heads-up to the HR team or even the whole company that company health needs to be improved.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Did you know that when new hires aren\'t as productive as they should be, it costs the company?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Yes – low productivity from new hires can cause companies to lose <a href=\"https://www.forcepersonnelok.com/2022/03/22/3-ways-to-control-hiring-costs/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">1-2.5% in revenue</a>. If the organization isn\'t tracking productivity, to begin with, it won\'t be aware of when new hires are taking longer than they should to become productive. The result? Revenue takes a hit.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>New Employee Performance</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Finally, time to productivity is a great metric to assess the performance of new employees.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>By tracking how long it takes for them to become productive, you can understand how well they have adjusted to their role or if they\'re having difficulties. This gives employers an opportunity to provide extra support and guidance where necessary while also recognizing good performance.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Multiple factors can affect the time it takes for a new hire to become productive, so it tends to vary from one organization to another. However, according to a <a href=\"https://www.gallup.com/workplace/247076/onboarding-new-employees-perspective-paper.aspx?thank-you-report-form=1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Gallup report</a>, 12 months is the average length of time it takes for a new employee to become fully productive. Relatively supporting that <a href=\"https://humanpanel.com/onboarding-and-new-hire-time-to-productivity/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Human Panel</a>, which says that it takes from 5-8 months for most new employees to reach full productivity.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In the majority of cases, there\'s something to be done to help make new hires productive quicker. The key lies in the below 5 factors, that if managed properly, can shift the needle in the right direction:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Company Culture</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There\'s no denying that the surrounding environment can impact a new hire’s productivity. Working in an environment that\'s too laid back can lead to a lack of focus while one that\'s too rigid can eventually cause burnout. It\'s important for employers to strike the right balance between structure and flexibility.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>On top of that, companies should foster open communication and encourage new hires to take ownership of their work, ask questions, and collaborate with their colleagues.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Training Required for Autonomy</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Not all job roles are created equal – some require more training than others before the new hire can become autonomous. It\'s important for organizations to be able to pinpoint the amount of training required depending on the role an individual is assigned to.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Generally speaking, the more <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/benefits-of-microlearning/\">focused training</a> a new hire needs, the longer it will take for them to become productive. However, it\'ll certainly happen faster than it would\'ve if the training programs didn\'t exist.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Onboarding Operations</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Onboarding programs make all the difference in how long or short time to productivity is – it\'s a fact. <a href=\"https://techjury.net/blog/onboarding-statistics/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">62% of companies</a> that have effective onboarding programs are seeing more employees reach full productivity faster and a <a href=\"https://techjury.net/blog/onboarding-statistics/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">54% increase</a> in employee engagement.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A well-structured, good onboarding program should involve a comprehensive introduction to the organization and its culture and processes. It should also include technical and soft skills training as well as assign clear objectives that new hires can focus on from day one. That kind of roadmap puts new hires on the path to success much quicker.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Company Size</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Company size isn\'t a factor many organizations consider, but company size does make a difference. Larger companies tend to have more complex roles and systems, which can slow down the learning process. Smaller companies, on the other hand, may be able to provide new hires with a clearer understanding of their role and tasks from Day 1.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>However, it\'s worth mentioning that size also translates into resources, with larger companies having more of them to support new hires during the onboarding process. It all boils down to the company\'s ability to provide concrete support and guidance during the onboarding process.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Amount of Support Available</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Last, but not least, it\'s one thing to throw new hires in the deep end and expect them to swim, but it\'s another to provide them with the necessary tools and support to help them cross the finish line.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This is why having dedicated onboarding mentors or coaches that can provide personalized, ongoing feedback, answer questions, and offer guidance is so important. This is especially true for roles that require complex skill sets or a deep understanding of company processes.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The higher the level of support available during onboarding, the faster new hires can become productive.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} -->
<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">\">Final Thoughts: New Hire Time to Productivity</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>So, it turns out that there\'s a way to effectively measure (objectively!) how quickly a newly hired employee becomes productive. Guesswork is no longer needed!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>That said, it\'s clear that the time to productivity is affected by a variety of factors, the most important being the onboarding process, which can easily make or break a new hire’s success. That means that onboarding programs now need to cover all the bases – from company culture and technical skills to expectations and support – in order to ensure that new hires become productive as efficiently as possible.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you\'re looking for a partner to help you maximize your onboarding success, we\'d love to hear from you! Feel free to book a <a href=\"https://www.figma.com/exit?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.ninjatropic.com%2Felearning-video-animation-companies-free-consultation%2F\">free consultation</a> call with us so that we can discuss the possibilities. We specialize in microlearning and eLearning content that can streamline your training initiatives and give your onboarding program the boost it needs. Let\'s get started!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'New Hire Time to Productivity: How to Improve Employee Performance', 'Reduce new hire time to productivity with effective strategies. Learn how to accelerate onboarding and enhance performance for business success.', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', 'new-hire-time-to-productivity', '', '', '2026-06-25 20:25:59', '2026-06-25 20:25:59', '', '0', 'http://localhost:8080/new-hire-time-to-productivity/', '0', 'post', '', '0'),
('2588', '0', '2026-06-05 22:54:11', '2026-06-05 22:54:11', 'New Hire Time to Productivity. From: New Hire Time to Productivity: How to Improve Employee Performance.', 'New Hire Time to Productivity', 'New Hire Time to Productivity', 'inherit', 'open', 'closed', '', 'new-hire-time-to-productivity-2', '', '', '2026-06-05 22:54:11', '2026-06-05 22:54:11', '', '2587', 'http://localhost:8080/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/new-hire-time-to-productivity.webp', '0', 'attachment', 'image/webp', '0'),
('2589', '7', '2023-07-20 10:47:35', '2023-07-20 17:47:35', '<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":1} -->
<h1>Interactive Video for eLearning: How to Engage Learners & Boost Results</h1>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Interactive video learning is not a static process. It\'s dynamic and fluid, and in the context of the modern world, learning processes are evolving every day.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Gone are the days of having to sit through a long-form lecture or reading a bulky book to acquire new information. eLearning and microlearning platforms have changed the game entirely.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title1\">Key Benefits of Interactive Video Learning</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title2\">Take Learners On a Journey With Interactive Videos</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title3\">Final Thoughts: Interactive Video for eLearning</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title4\">Interactive Video Learning FAQ</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Interactive video learning is a small yet notable part of the entire eLearning experience. By combining the immersion you get from a good story and the flexibility to learn on your own time from any of your own devices, a good interactive video can be extremely handy for training your employees.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>But leaving it at that won\'t be doing it proper justice. In this article, we\'ll talk about how you can benefit from interactive video-based learning and how you can engage learners and get credible results by using this powerful learning tool.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And once you understand what interactive video learning can do for you, why not book a<strong><a href=\"https://www.figma.com/exit?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.ninjatropic.com%2Felearning-video-animation-companies-free-consultation%2F\"> free consultation with us</a></strong> to help you strategize moving forward?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you want to integrate a valid eLearning strategy into your business that includes interactive videos and microlearning, then you need results. You don\'t want to sink your resources into making interactive videos if it doesn\'t bring you any output.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>So here are some of the main benefits that you can only get by using an interactive video for learning.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>1. Multi-Device Accessibility</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The biggest benefit of interactive video learning is that you have all your lessons on every device you own. And that means you get to access your lessons anywhere, any time. It really takes away any time constraints that you might have while acquiring new knowledge and information.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>We believe that flexibility is essential to a good learning experience. And having the interactive videos available on your smartphone, tablet, or laptop at the same time makes for a more accessible learning environment for the learners.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>2. Personalized Learning</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>With interactive video lessons, you can take a fully personalized approach to learning. What matters most here are the learner choices giving them complete freedom to explore their options. Learners can take on specific roles and fill their knowledge gaps through interactive lessons.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It\'s entirely dependent on the learners how much they want to focus on a specific subject or how far they want to branch out towards relevant topics. The user-driven decision-making format of interactive videos also increases the knowledge retention capabilities of the learner.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>3. Increase Learner Engagement</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Interactive videos have the power to keep the learners engaged in the course material by immersing them in a story. Of course, the interactive video content itself needs to be designed properly, but when the lesson is well-designed, interactive videos can keep the learners hooked.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Through interactive video-based learning, the learner can create a personal connection with the content and can create their own narrative through a decision-based learning experience. While gamification of learning materials is fun and exciting, interactive videos can take things to the next level.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>4. Flexibility</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As a learning module, interactive videos are extremely versatile. They can be designed as long-form content or can also be used to deliver short, efficient microlearning materials depending on your desired learning outcomes.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And designing the courses can also be done pretty fast and flexibly. While better production will often net better results, technically, as long as you have a video camera or smartphone and basic video editing software to edit the content, you can create engaging learning experiences quickly through interactive videos.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>5. Cost-Effective</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>For businesses, it\'s important to train employees without ramping up the training cost to an absurd level. And interactive video learning, because of its cost-effective nature, offers an excellent way to do exactly that.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Creating engaging videos to train employees shouldn\'t be too difficult with some practice. The <strong><a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/blog-how-much-does-an-elearning-video-cost/\">cost of creating an eLearning video</a></strong> considering the level of benefits it provides isn\'t much at all. Since it\'s easier to absorb new information through videos, your employees will also be able to pick up new skills much easier.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Research shows that employees are <strong><a href=\"https://elearningindustry.com/using-videos-in-corporate-training-strategy-2020\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">more likely to learn</a></strong> by watching a video rather than by reading a document or email.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The goal of creating an interactive video is not only to teach but to take your learners on a journey through realistic scenarios. Yes: it helps in acquiring skills and knowledge, but the more critical part is that it allows the employees to understand how to use the acquired skill in the real world.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The biggest strength of videos, interactive or not, is that it allows the viewer to visualize everything, and you need to use that to your advantage. Here\'s how you can get the most out of interactive videos.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>Interactive Storytelling</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>At the core of a solid interactive learning video, there\'s a good story. You should never underestimate the power of good storytelling. It will engage your learners better and improve their knowledge retention capability.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And when you\'re making an interactive video for your employees, make sure they are learning through a good story that they can use in the real world. This is the best way to hook your audience and help them acquire knowledge efficiently.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>Branched Videos</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Have you watched the new Black Mirror: Bandersnatch on Netflix? That\'s a good example of how branched videos work. Basically, with branched videos, the viewer is asked to actively participate in the narrative by choosing one path in different branching scenarios in the form of a pop-up screen in the video.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This lets the learner choose their own adventure and learn the outcome of their choice in a fun and controlled way. While it might seem daunting to design, there are many <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/interactive-video/\"><strong>helpful tools available</strong></a> these days to make things easier.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>Immersive Learning Experience</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You should aim to give your learners an immersive experience when designing interactive video learning content. It\'s not a slideshow, so don\'t be afraid to step out of your comfort zone and really connect with your students.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>An immersive experience goes beyond passive observation. By incorporating interactive elements, real-life scenarios, and engaging visuals, you can transport learners into an active and captivating educational journey.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>Learner Feedback & Analysis</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>These days, most, if not all, of the<strong> <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/best-microlearning-platforms/\">reputable microlearning platforms</a></strong> allow you to look at the feedback and monitor the performance of your employees. And when you\'re making an interactive video for them, taking a look at past analytics can provide fascinating insights into what elements the learners respond to better.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} -->
<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">\">\">Final Thoughts: Interactive Video for eLearning</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Training employees is an important part of a business. But the truth is tight budgets and deadlines can often get in the way of results. People can get demotivated, and with the<strong> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2019/apr/16/got-a-minute-global-attention-span-is-narrowing-study-reveals\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">short attention span becoming a real problem</a></strong>, it\'s important to take an efficient approach to learning in a corporate environment.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Using interactive videos for training employees is a step in the right direction and offers many benefits. What\'s more important is that it brings results while keeping the cost of training and learning from getting to an absurd level. It\'s a win-win for everyone!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>How Do I Make an Interactive Training Video?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The thought of creating an interactive training video might seem daunting at first, but if you follow the basic guidelines we talked about here, you should be fine. The first step is <strong><a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/blog-training-video-script-example/\">writing the video script</a></strong>, and you really don\'t want to rush that. Once you have that, the rest of the steps should come naturally.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>What Are Some Examples of Interactive Video?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Basically, any video that lets you interact with it in some capacity can be considered an interactive video. Non-interactive videos come with a couple of functions, such as stop, play, pause, rewind, fast forward, etc. But with an interactive video, you get to interact with the narrative itself in some way.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Black Mirror: Bandersnatch and Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt: Kimmy vs. The Reverend are two great examples of interactive video content. For corporate learning or employee training, elements such as quizzes or branching videos are often used as interactive components.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you\'re looking for a complete eLearning solution for your business, give Ninja Tropic a try, we\'ll provide you with a commitment-free sample plan that meets your objectives.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Are you aware of the sheer power of engaging eLearning solutions but not sure where to start?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Schedule a free 30-minute consultation with a Ninja Tropic expert to analyze your association, university, or enterprise’s content objectives and map out the interactive blueprint to achieve them.</p>
