<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title6\">Microlearning Platforms FAQ</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Before we talk shop, please have a look at these stats:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>TikTok users <a href=\"https://www.wired.co.uk/article/tiktok-wants-longer-videos-like-not\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">find videos longer</a> than 60 seconds stressful</li>
<li>Short-form videos popularity will soar in 2023, according to <a href=\"https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/hubspot-blog-marketing-industry-trends-report\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Hubspot</a></li>
<li>And <a href=\"https://www.forbes.com/sites/dbloom/2022/08/11/youtube-video-shorts-see-giant-jump-in-views-in-past-year/?sh=225b7b3133fc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">50% of YouTube views</a> are under 60 seconds (updated July 2022)</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Like it or not – this is a clear indication that human attention span has taken a big hit in recent years. So, if your business relies on once-tried-and-true training methods, it\'s likely to suffer.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>So, what\'s the solution?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Enter Microlearning Platforms.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>These platforms offer businesses and individuals the ability to take a smart approach to learning by breaking down existing content into small bite-sized pieces. As a result, <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/blog-how-to-plan-create-effective-employee-training-videos-step-by-step-guide/\">training employees</a> on new skills become much easier because they have more realistic knowledge checks.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And if you want to incorporate microlearning into your corporate L&D, exploring your options is always a great idea. That\'s why we\'ve decided to compare and talk about some of the best microlearning platforms for corporate learning.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Let\'s hop in!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>\"What\'s in a name?\"</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>While Shakespeare wanted to show that naming is irrelevant, when it comes to microlearning, it\'s all in the name.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Broken down to its very essence – micro = small, and learning = gaining knowledge.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>So, quick and small bursts of learning instead of the traditional consumption of a large chunk of information is microlearning.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Microlearning platforms can be mobile apps or websites that make learning content fun and engaging by:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>Creating bite-sized training material (<a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/blog-microlearning-video/\">videos</a>, texts, images)</li>
<li>Incorporating short quizzes to make the training process engaging</li>
<li>Gamifying learning content</li>
<li>And the one thing subpar microlearning platforms miss – having a very specific goal for each training</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The advantage of the microlearning approach is that learners can consume knowledge at a much quicker pace. A top-shelf microlearning platform makes learning fun and keeps learners hooked.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Online courses from microlearning platforms <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/benefits-of-microlearning/\">help businesses</a> in training their employees and capture new life skills by taking a path-based approach to learning. And more importantly, it also saves time and company resources.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Microlearning has come a long way since its conception. And with the \"<a href=\"https://time.com/3858309/attention-spans-goldfish/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Goldfish Effect</a>\" becoming a real problem, there\'s a risk of your employees getting lost or distracted in a maze of interactive content.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you want to get the most out of online training, you need to look for some essential features in your chosen microlearning platform.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Learning Curve </strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Software adoption can be a tough job for many individuals or even big businesses. Switching to a microlearning platform suddenly instead of the traditional process can take some time to get used to.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And if a microlearning app is hard to integrate into your business ecosystem, it\'s not going to do your employees any favors. That\'s why it\'s important to go with a platform that doesn\'t have a steep learning curve.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Time & Budget </strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You need to pick a platform that fits your budget and saves you time by delivering a complete library that you can use right away.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you want to make your own training courses, make sure you don\'t need to jump through a bunch of hoops to access simple features in the platform.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Current Software Setup</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you have an existing learning system for your employees, it\'s best to go with a platform that lets you build on it.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You don\'t want to throw away the material you already have.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Instead of taking a completely different approach to learning, all the best microlearning platforms enable you to improve upon existing content.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>LMS Features </strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>LMS, or Language Management System, is a digital environment to manage different training efforts.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And when you are choosing a platform to go with, you should look for LMS features like granular reporting, analytical capabilities, gamification, security, etc.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Goals & Objectives</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>What are you trying to get out of the platform or app?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>What\'s your desired end result?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Ask yourself these questions and try to figure out how a microlearning platform will help you achieve them.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And if you feel lost, you can always get a free consultation with an <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/elearning-video-animation-companies-free-consultation/\">eLearning solutions provider</a> to help you get back on track!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Microlearning is not free, and picking one platform that works for you can be hard if you don\'t do your homework. Here are some of the best platforms that are available for businesses and individuals.</p>
