('2810', '0', '2026-06-21 04:32:59', '2026-06-21 04:32:59', '<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":1} -->
<h1>Microlearning Examples & Best Practices to Boost Employee Engagement</h1>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Microlearning is a powerful tool for boosting employee development and engagement. Think bite-sized lessons, easily digestible, and perfect for today\'s busy workforce. It\'s learning that fits right into the flow of work.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>By delivering information in small, digestible chunks, microlearning makes it easier for employees to access, learn and retain new skills. This approach is particularly effective for today\'s busy workforce, who often struggle to find time for traditional training.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title1\">What is Microlearning Content?</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title2\">Why Microlearning?</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title3\">Key Benefits of Microlearning</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title4\">11 Microlearning Examples for Modern Learners in 2023</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title5\">Final Thoughts: Examples of Microlearning</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This article provides practical microlearning examples and short video overviews. <strong>We\'re also excited to announce the launch of the Microlearning Lab YouTube channel!</strong> This channel is your one-stop shop for everything microlearning. We\'ll share expert insights, real-world case studies, and practical tips to help you transform your training.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>To get inspired and learn more about microlearning and digital learning, check out the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@microlearningexamples\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Microlearning Lab YouTube channel</a>. Their channel offers a wealth of resources, insight from leading experts, and examples to help you create engaging and effective microlearning experiences.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} -->
<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">\">What is microlearning?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Microlearning is a training approach that delivers information in small, focused bursts to maximize memory retention. It\'s designed to cater to the preferences of modern learners who have short attention spans and prefer quick, digestible content. Microlearning can take many forms: short videos, quizzes, infographics, or even simple text messages.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Modern learners are used to consuming social medium information in bite sized chunks. They expect content to be visually appealing, interactive, and mobile-friendly. Microlearning meets these expectations by delivering content in a format that is easy to consume and digest.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} -->
<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why consider microlearning?</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The modern workplace is fast-paced. Employees need training that\'s quick, relevant, and easy to access. Microlearning fits the bill perfectly. It\'s designed for on-the-go learning, making it ideal for today\'s mobile workforce.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Microlearning is a fantastic way to boost memory retention and skill development. By breaking down complex topics into smaller, easily digestible chunks, it makes learning more efficient and enjoyable. Imagine being able to learn new skills quickly and easily, fitting training into even the busiest schedules.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Microlearning is the perfect solution for organizations looking to enhance their training programs and improve employee performance. It is becoming a growing trend on <a href=\"https://trends.google.com/trends/explore?date=2010-07-03%202024-08-03&geo=US&q=microlearning&hl=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">google searches by learners and companies looking to deploy a microlearning strategy. </a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} -->
<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Benefits of microlearning</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Microlearning\'s short form accessible nature, like videos, boosts learner motivation and active participation. This approach aligns with the way people naturally learn and process information, making training more enjoyable and engaging. A study by Software Advice found that 58% of employees would be more likely to use their company\'s learning tools if the content was broken down into multiple, shorter lessons.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The bite sized format of microlearning aligns with how our brains naturally process information. Short bursts of focused content are easier to absorb and remember compared to lengthy training sessions. Research by Hermann Ebbinghaus, a pioneer in memory studies, suggests that people forget up to 90% of new information within a month, but spaced repetition, a key feature of microlearning, can significantly improve retention. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spaced_repetition\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spaced Repetition – Ebbinghaus</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Microlearning\'s flexibility empowers learners to access training on their own terms. Whether it\'s during a commute, a lunch break, or before bed, learners can fit learning into their busy schedules. This accessibility accommodates different learning styles and preferences, leading to greater engagement and better outcomes. A survey by Deloitte found that 75% of employees prefer personalized learning experiences, and microlearning fits that bill perfectly. <a href=\"https://www2.deloitte.com/us/en/insights/focus/human-capital-trends/2019.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Deloitte – Personalized Learning</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} -->
<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Microlearning Examples</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Microlearning, with its short, focused bursts of information, has become a cornerstone of effective employee training. To illustrate the versatility of this approach, we\'ve curated a series of microlearning examples across various industries. From healthcare to technology, finance to retail, you\'ll discover how microlearning is revolutionizing training programs and driving performance improvement.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>👉 Check out the <strong><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@microlearningexamples\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Microlearning Lab YouTube channel</a>. </strong>You can find a ton of great resources and Microlearning examples. 👈</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Learn how to quickly update your medication knowledge or master new treatment protocols with concise training modules.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Get up to speed on the latest software features or coding techniques through short, engaging lessons.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Understand complex financial rules or explore new investment strategies with easy-to-digest training</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Enhance product knowledge or learn effective sales techniques through quick, interactive training.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Boost safety awareness or master new equipment operation with brief, informative modules.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Quick interactive animation demonstrates safety training in a format that resonates with the learners.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A series of interactive videos introduces new hires to the company\'s core values through relatable stories.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A microlearning module offers tips and scenarios for giving constructive feedback in a positive way.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A step-by-step visual guide helps older customers learn how to use a new online social media feature.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>An animated microlearning video on cyber fraud prevention with nontechnical users.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Understand new policies or improve public service delivery with concise, informative training.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Learn how to handle customers or master customer interaction with an effective microlearning-based training course</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} -->
<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Microlearning best practices</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>👉 Explore our <strong><a href=\"https://youtube.com/playlist?list=PLfU4pcS-OLnxrX8IvKt3H2exDKTSB54XT&si=Pl-XG8pn5wMk03TW\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Microlearning Lab Best Practices playlist</a></strong> for in-depth guidance on creating engaging and effective microlearning experiences.👈</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Microlearning is all about brevity. Each module should focus on a single, clear learning objective. Avoid information overload; instead, deliver content in small, easily digestible chunks. Remember, the goal is to provide quick, impactful learning experiences.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Today\'s workforce is constantly on the go. Ensure your microlearning content is accessible and optimized for mobile devices. This allows employees to learn anytime, anywhere, fitting training into their busy schedules.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Dull content doesn’t cut it in the microlearning world. Use interactive elements like hotspots, simulations, and gamification to keep learners engaged. Incorporate visuals, such as images, videos, or infographics, to enhance understanding and retention.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Tailor your microlearning content to specific job roles and performance needs. By addressing real-world challenges, you increase the likelihood of knowledge transfer and application. Align your modules with overall business goals to maximize their impact.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Track learner engagement and performance metrics to evaluate the effectiveness of your microlearning program. Use data to identify areas for improvement and make adjustments as needed. Continuously refine your content to ensure it meets the evolving needs of your employees.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} -->
<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Microlearning Strategy</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A successful microlearning strategy is all about focus and impact. Pinpoint specific skills or knowledge gaps within your organization and deliver targeted, bite-sized learning experiences. Combine microlearning with traditional training for a powerful learning approach. Regularly measure how well your microlearning works and make improvements based on the data.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} -->
<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Microlearning Videos</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Short, focused videos are a fantastic way to share information and engage your audience. Whether you\'re training employees or educating customers, microlearning videos can make a big difference. Use them to explain complex topics simply, demonstrate processes, or reinforce key points. By making learning accessible and enjoyable, you can boost employee satisfaction and customer loyalty.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Here\'s why microlearning videos are a top choice:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li><strong>Versatility:</strong> They can be used for a wide range of topics and audiences.</li>
<li><strong>Engagement:</strong> Visuals and audio keep learners interested and focused.</li>
<li><strong>Accessibility:</strong> Easily accessible on various devices for on-the-go learning.</li>
<li><strong>Retention:</strong> Visuals aid in memory and recall of information.</li>
<li><strong>Cost-Effective:</strong> Relatively inexpensive to produce and distribute.</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} -->
<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Learning Experience Design</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Microlearning offers a compelling solution to the challenges of modern workplace learning. By delivering concise, focused content, it effectively addresses the short attention spans and time constraints of today\'s employees. This approach maximizes knowledge retention and skill development, ensuring that learning directly impacts job performance.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Good microlearning aligns with the principles of adult learning. It respects learners\' prior knowledge and experience, providing opportunities for skill enhancement and performance improvement. By offering flexibility and control over the learning process, microlearning boosts employee engagement and motivation. This leads to a more positive learning experience, fostering a culture of continuous improvement within the organization.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>Enhanced Learning Outcomes and Engagement</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Microlearning has demonstrated a significant impact on learning outcomes and employee engagement. A LinkedIn Learning Report found that short, focused learning segments can boost retention by 20% and increase employee engagement by 50%. This aligns with research from the Journal of Applied Psychology, which shows that breaking down complex topics improves comprehension and knowledge application.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>Increased Efficiency and Cost Savings</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Organizations are increasingly turning to microlearning to streamline their training processes. Bersin by Deloitte reports a 300% increase in development speed and up to 50% cost savings for companies using microlearning. The Association for Talent Development (ATD) supports this, stating that microlearning can reduce training time by 60% without sacrificing learning outcomes.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>Positive Impact on Employee Performance and Satisfaction</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Beyond learning efficiency, microlearning positively impacts employee performance and satisfaction. Brandon Hall Group research indicates a 50% boost in employee engagement and a 17% increase in job satisfaction when microlearning is implemented. SafetyCulture emphasizes the practical application of microlearning, highlighting its role in enhancing operational efficiency and reducing training costs.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>Growing Adoption and Research</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The effectiveness of microlearning has gained significant attention. A TechTrends bibliometric analysis reveals a surge in microlearning research, particularly post-COVID-19, as organizations sought efficient training solutions. Moreover, eLearning Industry reports a high adoption rate, with 98% of organizations planning to continue using microlearning due to its positive impact.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Shift Learning underscores the power of microlearning in boosting retention rates (up to 60%) and achieving high completion rates (82%), making it a compelling choice for organizations seeking to optimize their learning strategies.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Ultimately, microlearning is a strategic investment in human capital. By optimizing the learning experience, organizations can enhance employee performance, productivity, and satisfaction. This approach is essential for staying competitive in today\'s rapidly evolving business landscape.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} -->
<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">\">Challenges of microlearning</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Developing good microlearning content can be challenging and creating concise, impactful learning modules requires careful planning and design. Balancing depth of information with brevity is a delicate task.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Measuring the impact of microlearning can be difficult. Traditional training methods often rely on pre and post-tests, but these might not be suitable for the short format of microlearning. Finding alternative methods to assess knowledge retention and skill improvement is essential.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Maintaining consistency in quality across multiple microlearning modules is another hurdle. Ensuring that all content adheres to the same design standards and learning objectives can be time-consuming. Managing the creation and distribution of numerous small modules can also be logistically challenging.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Integrating microlearning into existing<strong> <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/lms-management-services-the-challenge-of-filling-the-lms-role/\">learning management systems (LMS)</a> </strong>can present technical difficulties. Adapting the LMS to accommodate short-form content and tracking learner progress effectively might require additional development or customization.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Cost-effectiveness is a crucial consideration. While microlearning can be efficient, producing high-quality content requires resources. Balancing the need for engaging, interactive modules with budgetary constraints can be challenging.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Developing effective microlearning content is no small feat. Creating concise, impactful learning modules requires careful planning and design. Balancing depth of information with brevity can be tricky. Ensuring consistency across multiple modules is another hurdle. Integrating microlearning into existing learning management systems can also pose challenges. And finally, measuring the impact of microlearning can be complex.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Overcoming these challenges requires careful planning and the right tools. By investing in a robust authoring tool and leveraging data analytics, organizations can create engaging and effective microlearning experiences.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Are you ready to explore the potential of microlearning? <strong><a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/elearning-video-animation-companies-free-consultation/\">Contact us to learn how we can help you overcome these challenges.</a></strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'Microlearning Examples: Boost Your Corporate Training Program', 'Practical microlearning examples for corporate L&#038;D and employee engagement. Learn how to create engaging bite-sized training that gets results.', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '2583-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-06-21 04:32:59', '2026-06-21 04:32:59', '', '2583', 'http://localhost:8080/?p=2810', '0', 'revision', '', '0'),
('2811', '0', '2026-06-21 04:33:04', '2026-06-21 04:33:04', '<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":1} -->
<h1>eLearning Interactivity 2023: The 4 Levels & How to Use Them (Plus Benefits)</h1>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Whether it\'s school, university, or the workplace, learning is always more engaging when it\'s interactive. Think about it: if you have to sit through a long lecture or reading session, wouldn\'t you enjoy it more if you got to do something with your hands, like complete a puzzle, or be part of a role-playing game or simulation?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title1\">What Is eLearning Interactivity?</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title2\">What Are the Four Levels of Interactivity in eLearning?</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title3\">What Are the Benefits of Interactivity in eLearning?</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title4\">How to Make Interactive eLearning Courses?</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title5\">Final Thoughts: Improving the Learning Process With Interactivity</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The same applies to eLearning. Just because it\'s an online course doesn\'t mean you can\'t use interactive elements to improve engagement and retain knowledge. We can even go as far as saying that there\'s room for interactivity in eLearning that doesn\'t exist in traditional classrooms!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In this guide, we\'ll be taking a high-level look at the 4 levels of interactivity in eLearning, what they mean, and how you can take advantage of them to create an engaging learning experience. We\'ll also explore the benefits that come with interactive eLearning content so you can make a case for investing in it.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When eLearning interactivity is mentioned, it refers to learning mechanisms that aim to engage learners with the content and learning process. Rather than passive learning, learners interact with the content in some way—usually by either doing or thinking.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/interactive-video-for-elearning/\">Interactivity in eLearning</a> can take many forms, ranging from simple tasks such as clicking a button to more advanced ones, such as multiple-choice quizzes, tests, simulations, and more. Ultimately, the goal of interactive eLearning is to help the user build a better understanding of the subject matter through active, rather than passive, interaction.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There are four main levels of eLearning interactivity: passive, limited, moderate, and full. Here\'s a look at each in more detail.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>1. Passive eLearning Interactivity</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>At the most basic level, there\'s passive interactivity. This is where learners are only presented with information and can\'t change or affect it in any way. Think of this as being similar to sitting in a traditional classroom and simply listening to a lecture—you can take notes, but there\'s no way to interact with the content.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This level is often referred to as the \"click next\" or \"page turner\" style because learners are only asked to click a button or turn the page to continue to the next piece of content in a linear fashion.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Interactivity-wise, there are simple elements such as images or graphics, simple video and audio, and straightforward multiple-choice or true-or-false questions, but without any further interactivity beyond clicking.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>2. Limited eLearning Interactivity</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The next level involves limited interaction. While it\'s still relatively simple, it allows the user to do more than just click a button. Think of this as requiring learners to complete some sort of action to advance, such as drag-and-drop interactions, matching labels with images, click-and-reveal, or typing in a response.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>At this level, the content is kept simple and learners are only asked to complete basic interactions that don\'t require deep levels of understanding. This style of eLearning is great for introductory courses or those that build on knowledge from previous experiences.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Content-wise, the material includes clickable animated graphics, navigation that expands to menus, glossaries, external resources, and audio and video.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>3. Moderate eLearning Interactivity</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Moving up one level brings us to moderate interactivity. Here, the content is more dynamic because it\'s designed with branching scenarios—or what some call \"non-linear learning\"—that allow learners to explore multiple paths and receive feedback through different levels.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Because moderate interactivity is best for teaching learners complex skills, you\'ll want to include a high level of complexity and customization in your course. This might include scenario-based cases, complex simulations, <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/blog-the-5-e-learning-video-animation-styles/\">custom flash animations</a>, stories, and other forms of multimedia.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>4. Full eLearning Interactivity</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Finally, full interactivity represents the highest level of engagement. Think of levels 1, 2, and 3 as a pyramid, with the apex representing full immersion. The courses at this level include all of the components in other levels, plus gamification or simulation. These range from 360° images and avatars to interactive videos, stories, scenarios, and more.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Learners are also kept motivated throughout the course with a reward system. This could be points, badges, levels, leaderboards—whatever motivates your learners!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Full interactivity also includes complex branching scenarios that allow for open-ended decision-making. Learners receive feedback based on their choices, and the outcomes can change depending on what they decide. In other words, their learning path is created as they go, and no two paths are the same.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This level is ideal for learners who need to practice real-time decision-making skills, and results in the most immersive learning experience. Although these courses take more time to design and develop, they\'re worth it—for both you and your learners.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Interactive learning brings about a number of benefits that static learning lacks. Here are a few of the biggest advantages you\'ll gain when you add interactivity to your eLearning environment:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>1. Boosts Engagement for Learners</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Rather than learners staring at the screen passively with their minds wandering to other topics, interactivity switches that to active learning by stimulating their attention and keeping them interested in the material and the learning environment – all through providing them with something to either think of or do.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>2. Encourages Reflection</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When we\'re asked a question, we naturally reflect on our response and assess before speaking, right? Interactive eLearning encourages learners to do just that by providing learners with prompts and interactive activities. This helps establish a deeper understanding as they reflect on the material they\'ve been presented with while fostering self-assessment and critical thinking skills.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>3. Knowledge Retention</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If someone tells you a piece of information as is–with no interaction on your part–the chances of you remembering it are slim to none. But how about if it was presented to you as a game, or in the form of a scenario or story? You\'d be <a href=\"https://medium.com/universal-storyteller/why-stories-are-memorable-4b42250e997b\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">more likely to remember it</a>, right? That\'s because when you engage with something through interactivity, your brain is more likely to store that information away for future recall.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Interactive eLearning encourages knowledge retention by engaging the learner, prompting them to think critically about the material and utilize their decision-making skills. As they progress through the course, learners are given the opportunity to reflect on what they\'ve learned and make connections between the material presented while furthering their understanding of it.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The result? Increased knowledge retention that leads to a better understanding of the material and, eventually, improved performance.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>4. Emotionally Stimulating</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Nowadays, people are more emotionally stimulated by information and multimedia than ever before, and it\'s only when they have an emotional response that they truly remember it. Otherwise, it\'s just another piece of information among the countless incoming information in our minds on a daily basis.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Interactive eLearning takes this idea and runs with it by incorporating different elements that evoke emotion in the learner: meaningful stories, interesting visuals, powerful value statements, shocking statistics, confrontational questions, and more. And when emotions are involved, attention is held, action is taken, and behavior is changed.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>5. Promotes Motivation</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Learning isn\'t always fun, and motivation levels can quickly drop when learners are faced with mundane tasks. That\'s why it\'s important to inject some “fun” elements into your eLearning courses, such as multimedia, interactive scenarios, and games. The more interesting a story or an eLearning game, the more motivated learners will be to participate in the eLearning process – willingly.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The keyword here is “engagement.” Learner engagement and motivation go hand in hand, meaning that the more engaged learners are, the easier it will be for them to stay motivated and complete the course.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>6. Triggers Application</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Lastly, interactive eLearning increases learners’ ability to apply the knowledge they\'ve acquired. The more engaging and immersive your courses are, the better the chances of learners applying them in their day-to-day life.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Interactive eLearning gives learners a chance to practice what they\'ve learned in an environment that\'s as close to real life as possible, allowing them to be creative and explore all of their options through trial and error. By doing so, learners gain experience and become more confident in their abilities.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>With that said, here are a few ideas to give you a head start when creating interactive eLearning courses:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Try Out Sneak Peeks and Teasers</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Entice your learners with sneak previews of the course they\'re about to take. Tease them by giving out small pieces of information that will make them want to learn more. This strategy helps to stir up interest and build anticipation before getting into the actual course content.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Make the Content Visually Appealing</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/blog-the-ultimate-guide-for-hiring-freelance-animators/\">Animations</a>, images, GIFs, and videos are all great ways to make eLearning courses more interactive and visually appealing. Visuals can help break up the monotony of reading text on a screen, making the whole experience much more enjoyable for learners.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Use Onboarding Checklists</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Onboarding checklists are a great way to get learners more engaged with the material. Providing small tasks that they can complete and check off, gives them the incentive to stay focused on the course and encourages them to take action from the start. There\'s something about checking off a task that just makes it seem more rewarding.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Incorporate Interactive Maps and Charts</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Interactive maps and charts help learners visualize the subject matter more easily, making it easier to understand. Instead of reading a long block of text with facts and figures, interactive charts allow learners to instantly decipher the information in a much more digestible way.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Include Games and Puzzles</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Games and puzzles are an excellent way to keep learners engaged for longer periods. They can also be used as a form of assessment, testing the learner’s knowledge of the content and allowing them to practice problem-solving skills.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Always Gauge Feedback</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Finally, a great way to ensure that your learners are engaged and understand the content is to regularly ask for feedback. This can be done through surveys, informal Q&A sessions, or other methods. Gathering feedback allows you to adjust the course content in real-time according to the needs of the learners.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} -->
<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">\">Final Thoughts: Improving the Learning Process With Interactivity</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>At the end of the day, interactive eLearning has the power to take the learning process to a whole new level. It adds a sense of purpose that motivates learners to stay engaged and puts them in full control of their progress. And when that happens, there\'s no stopping them from becoming the best version of themselves.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Yes, this may mean you\'ll need to work a bit harder in creating engaging eLearning resources, but the results are worth it. And the best part is: you don\'t have to go it alone. At Ninja Tropic, eLearning is our specialty and we have the experience and tools to make your interactive courses come alive. <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/contact-us/\">Contact us</a> to learn about how we can help you take your eLearning game to the next level! Or <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/elearning-video-animation-companies-free-consultation/\">book a free consultation</a> to get your complimentary sample plan today!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'eLearning Interactivity 2023: The 4 Levels & How to Use Them (Plus Benefits)', 'Boost engagement with eLearning interactivity. Discover how interactive elements transform learning experiences for better retention and enjoyment.', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '2585-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-06-21 04:33:04', '2026-06-21 04:33:04', '', '2585', 'http://localhost:8080/?p=2811', '0', 'revision', '', '0'),
('2812', '0', '2026-06-21 04:33:11', '2026-06-21 04:33:11', '<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":1} -->
<h1>New Hire Time to Productivity: How to Improve Employee Performance</h1>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>After organizations spend months-on-end in the hiring process, searching for the right candidate, right on the new hire\'s first day, they already have one question in mind:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>\"When will I start to see results?\"</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title1\">What Is New Hire Time to Productivity?</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title2\">How Can New Hire Time to Productivity Be Tracked?</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title3\">Why Track New Hires Time to Productivity?</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title4\">How Long Until Employees Are Fully Productive?</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title5\">Time to Productivity Contributing Factors</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title6\">Final Thoughts: New Hire Time to Productivity</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Performance expectations are high, and there\'s often pressure to get newly-hired employees up and running as soon as possible. Understandably, today\'s world of ever-increasing competition and shrinking margins has put greater emphasis on the need to maximize performance from day one.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>But without proper employee productivity metrics to track performance, evaluations are often subjective (mostly a pure guessing game!), and managers can’t always identify which new hire onboarding strategies are working best.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>That\'s where measuring new hire time to productivity comes in. Here\'s what you need to know about it.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>New hire time to productivity is a measurement of how long it takes for an employee to go from onboarding to being fully productive and meeting performance goals. In other words, it\'s the time a new employee takes to start adding value to the company from the day they start working.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This metric is used to measure the effectiveness of onboarding strategies, and it can help managers have an objective view of how well their new-hire training and onboarding strategies are performing. That\'s because supporting new employees from the get-go helps them become productive faster, and in turn, reduces time to productivity.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When it comes to how to measure time to productivity, there are a number of methods that organizations can use. However, the most common one is by subtracting the employee\'s start date from the date they become fully productive.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Similarly, to get the total average time of new hire time to productivity, organizations can track multiple employees at once by adding the total number of days for all new hires to reach full productivity over a given time frame and dividing it by the total number of new hires.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>For this to work, managers should create performance goals for new hires that must be met in a certain period of time- usually within the first few weeks or months of employment (<a href=\"https://seismic.com/blog/employee-onboarding-software-15-employee-engagement-stats/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">60% of companies</a> don\'t bother setting milestones or goals for new hires, so this is crucial.)</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This could range from completing specific certifications or <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/blog-how-to-plan-create-effective-employee-training-videos-step-by-step-guide/\">training videos</a> to reaching certain role-related performance targets, such as hitting a certain sales target or reaching a customer satisfaction score.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Then, measure how long it took them to reach those goals and calculate their time to productivity.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This metric can then be used to compare new hires and see how their onboarding experience is impacting their productivity. This can also be used to spot any areas of improvement and help HR leaders tweak their onboarding programs accordingly to maximize efficiency.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Pro Tip: To unify the calculation of time to productivity, it helps if the organization has a very clear definition of what “full productivity” means. This will provide everyone with an understanding of the expected goals and performance standards for new hires, making it easier to track their time to productivity and measure overall success.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Using the new hire productivity metric isn\'t only used to evaluate whether new employees are becoming productive or not. It can also be used to inform various HR decisions, providing insights into the following.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Onboarding Process Efficiency</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The general rule is that the faster a new hire becomes productive, the more effective the onboarding process is. Tracking time to productivity can help organizations determine if their current onboarding program is efficient or not. Most times, the \"standard\" onboarding process ends up hindering new employees from becoming productive faster.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Company Health</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Onboarding isn\'t the only factor that affects the time to productivity. If an organization is confident in its onboarding program yet it\'s still experiencing long times to productivity, it could be an indication of deeper issues within the organization.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Such issues could include unclear goals or a broken culture – all of which can affect new employees just as much as onboarding. As such, this could give a heads-up to the HR team or even the whole company that company health needs to be improved.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Did you know that when new hires aren\'t as productive as they should be, it costs the company?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Yes – low productivity from new hires can cause companies to lose <a href=\"https://www.forcepersonnelok.com/2022/03/22/3-ways-to-control-hiring-costs/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">1-2.5% in revenue</a>. If the organization isn\'t tracking productivity, to begin with, it won\'t be aware of when new hires are taking longer than they should to become productive. The result? Revenue takes a hit.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>New Employee Performance</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Finally, time to productivity is a great metric to assess the performance of new employees.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>By tracking how long it takes for them to become productive, you can understand how well they have adjusted to their role or if they\'re having difficulties. This gives employers an opportunity to provide extra support and guidance where necessary while also recognizing good performance.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Multiple factors can affect the time it takes for a new hire to become productive, so it tends to vary from one organization to another. However, according to a <a href=\"https://www.gallup.com/workplace/247076/onboarding-new-employees-perspective-paper.aspx?thank-you-report-form=1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Gallup report</a>, 12 months is the average length of time it takes for a new employee to become fully productive. Relatively supporting that <a href=\"https://humanpanel.com/onboarding-and-new-hire-time-to-productivity/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Human Panel</a>, which says that it takes from 5-8 months for most new employees to reach full productivity.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In the majority of cases, there\'s something to be done to help make new hires productive quicker. The key lies in the below 5 factors, that if managed properly, can shift the needle in the right direction:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Company Culture</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There\'s no denying that the surrounding environment can impact a new hire’s productivity. Working in an environment that\'s too laid back can lead to a lack of focus while one that\'s too rigid can eventually cause burnout. It\'s important for employers to strike the right balance between structure and flexibility.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>On top of that, companies should foster open communication and encourage new hires to take ownership of their work, ask questions, and collaborate with their colleagues.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Training Required for Autonomy</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Not all job roles are created equal – some require more training than others before the new hire can become autonomous. It\'s important for organizations to be able to pinpoint the amount of training required depending on the role an individual is assigned to.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Generally speaking, the more <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/benefits-of-microlearning/\">focused training</a> a new hire needs, the longer it will take for them to become productive. However, it\'ll certainly happen faster than it would\'ve if the training programs didn\'t exist.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Onboarding Operations</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Onboarding programs make all the difference in how long or short time to productivity is – it\'s a fact. <a href=\"https://techjury.net/blog/onboarding-statistics/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">62% of companies</a> that have effective onboarding programs are seeing more employees reach full productivity faster and a <a href=\"https://techjury.net/blog/onboarding-statistics/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">54% increase</a> in employee engagement.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>A well-structured, good onboarding program should involve a comprehensive introduction to the organization and its culture and processes. It should also include technical and soft skills training as well as assign clear objectives that new hires can focus on from day one. That kind of roadmap puts new hires on the path to success much quicker.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Company Size</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Company size isn\'t a factor many organizations consider, but company size does make a difference. Larger companies tend to have more complex roles and systems, which can slow down the learning process. Smaller companies, on the other hand, may be able to provide new hires with a clearer understanding of their role and tasks from Day 1.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>However, it\'s worth mentioning that size also translates into resources, with larger companies having more of them to support new hires during the onboarding process. It all boils down to the company\'s ability to provide concrete support and guidance during the onboarding process.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Amount of Support Available</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Last, but not least, it\'s one thing to throw new hires in the deep end and expect them to swim, but it\'s another to provide them with the necessary tools and support to help them cross the finish line.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This is why having dedicated onboarding mentors or coaches that can provide personalized, ongoing feedback, answer questions, and offer guidance is so important. This is especially true for roles that require complex skill sets or a deep understanding of company processes.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The higher the level of support available during onboarding, the faster new hires can become productive.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} -->
<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">\">Final Thoughts: New Hire Time to Productivity</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>So, it turns out that there\'s a way to effectively measure (objectively!) how quickly a newly hired employee becomes productive. Guesswork is no longer needed!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>That said, it\'s clear that the time to productivity is affected by a variety of factors, the most important being the onboarding process, which can easily make or break a new hire’s success. That means that onboarding programs now need to cover all the bases – from company culture and technical skills to expectations and support – in order to ensure that new hires become productive as efficiently as possible.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you\'re looking for a partner to help you maximize your onboarding success, we\'d love to hear from you! Feel free to book a <a href=\"https://www.figma.com/exit?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.ninjatropic.com%2Felearning-video-animation-companies-free-consultation%2F\">free consultation</a> call with us so that we can discuss the possibilities. We specialize in microlearning and eLearning content that can streamline your training initiatives and give your onboarding program the boost it needs. Let\'s get started!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'New Hire Time to Productivity: How to Improve Employee Performance', 'Reduce new hire time to productivity with effective strategies. Learn how to accelerate onboarding and enhance performance for business success.', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '2587-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-06-21 04:33:11', '2026-06-21 04:33:11', '', '2587', 'http://localhost:8080/?p=2812', '0', 'revision', '', '0'),
('2813', '0', '2026-06-21 04:33:16', '2026-06-21 04:33:16', '<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":1} -->
<h1>Interactive Video for eLearning: How to Engage Learners & Boost Results</h1>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Interactive video learning is not a static process. It\'s dynamic and fluid, and in the context of the modern world, learning processes are evolving every day.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Gone are the days of having to sit through a long-form lecture or reading a bulky book to acquire new information. eLearning and microlearning platforms have changed the game entirely.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title1\">Key Benefits of Interactive Video Learning</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title2\">Take Learners On a Journey With Interactive Videos</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title3\">Final Thoughts: Interactive Video for eLearning</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title4\">Interactive Video Learning FAQ</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Interactive video learning is a small yet notable part of the entire eLearning experience. By combining the immersion you get from a good story and the flexibility to learn on your own time from any of your own devices, a good interactive video can be extremely handy for training your employees.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>But leaving it at that won\'t be doing it proper justice. In this article, we\'ll talk about how you can benefit from interactive video-based learning and how you can engage learners and get credible results by using this powerful learning tool.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And once you understand what interactive video learning can do for you, why not book a<strong><a href=\"https://www.figma.com/exit?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.ninjatropic.com%2Felearning-video-animation-companies-free-consultation%2F\"> free consultation with us</a></strong> to help you strategize moving forward?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you want to integrate a valid eLearning strategy into your business that includes interactive videos and microlearning, then you need results. You don\'t want to sink your resources into making interactive videos if it doesn\'t bring you any output.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>So here are some of the main benefits that you can only get by using an interactive video for learning.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>1. Multi-Device Accessibility</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The biggest benefit of interactive video learning is that you have all your lessons on every device you own. And that means you get to access your lessons anywhere, any time. It really takes away any time constraints that you might have while acquiring new knowledge and information.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>We believe that flexibility is essential to a good learning experience. And having the interactive videos available on your smartphone, tablet, or laptop at the same time makes for a more accessible learning environment for the learners.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>2. Personalized Learning</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>With interactive video lessons, you can take a fully personalized approach to learning. What matters most here are the learner choices giving them complete freedom to explore their options. Learners can take on specific roles and fill their knowledge gaps through interactive lessons.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It\'s entirely dependent on the learners how much they want to focus on a specific subject or how far they want to branch out towards relevant topics. The user-driven decision-making format of interactive videos also increases the knowledge retention capabilities of the learner.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>3. Increase Learner Engagement</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Interactive videos have the power to keep the learners engaged in the course material by immersing them in a story. Of course, the interactive video content itself needs to be designed properly, but when the lesson is well-designed, interactive videos can keep the learners hooked.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Through interactive video-based learning, the learner can create a personal connection with the content and can create their own narrative through a decision-based learning experience. While gamification of learning materials is fun and exciting, interactive videos can take things to the next level.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>4. Flexibility</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As a learning module, interactive videos are extremely versatile. They can be designed as long-form content or can also be used to deliver short, efficient microlearning materials depending on your desired learning outcomes.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And designing the courses can also be done pretty fast and flexibly. While better production will often net better results, technically, as long as you have a video camera or smartphone and basic video editing software to edit the content, you can create engaging learning experiences quickly through interactive videos.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>5. Cost-Effective</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>For businesses, it\'s important to train employees without ramping up the training cost to an absurd level. And interactive video learning, because of its cost-effective nature, offers an excellent way to do exactly that.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Creating engaging videos to train employees shouldn\'t be too difficult with some practice. The <strong><a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/blog-how-much-does-an-elearning-video-cost/\">cost of creating an eLearning video</a></strong> considering the level of benefits it provides isn\'t much at all. Since it\'s easier to absorb new information through videos, your employees will also be able to pick up new skills much easier.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Research shows that employees are <strong><a href=\"https://elearningindustry.com/using-videos-in-corporate-training-strategy-2020\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">more likely to learn</a></strong> by watching a video rather than by reading a document or email.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The goal of creating an interactive video is not only to teach but to take your learners on a journey through realistic scenarios. Yes: it helps in acquiring skills and knowledge, but the more critical part is that it allows the employees to understand how to use the acquired skill in the real world.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The biggest strength of videos, interactive or not, is that it allows the viewer to visualize everything, and you need to use that to your advantage. Here\'s how you can get the most out of interactive videos.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>Interactive Storytelling</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>At the core of a solid interactive learning video, there\'s a good story. You should never underestimate the power of good storytelling. It will engage your learners better and improve their knowledge retention capability.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And when you\'re making an interactive video for your employees, make sure they are learning through a good story that they can use in the real world. This is the best way to hook your audience and help them acquire knowledge efficiently.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>Branched Videos</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Have you watched the new Black Mirror: Bandersnatch on Netflix? That\'s a good example of how branched videos work. Basically, with branched videos, the viewer is asked to actively participate in the narrative by choosing one path in different branching scenarios in the form of a pop-up screen in the video.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This lets the learner choose their own adventure and learn the outcome of their choice in a fun and controlled way. While it might seem daunting to design, there are many <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/interactive-video/\"><strong>helpful tools available</strong></a> these days to make things easier.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>Immersive Learning Experience</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You should aim to give your learners an immersive experience when designing interactive video learning content. It\'s not a slideshow, so don\'t be afraid to step out of your comfort zone and really connect with your students.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>An immersive experience goes beyond passive observation. By incorporating interactive elements, real-life scenarios, and engaging visuals, you can transport learners into an active and captivating educational journey.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>Learner Feedback & Analysis</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>These days, most, if not all, of the<strong> <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/best-microlearning-platforms/\">reputable microlearning platforms</a></strong> allow you to look at the feedback and monitor the performance of your employees. And when you\'re making an interactive video for them, taking a look at past analytics can provide fascinating insights into what elements the learners respond to better.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} -->
<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">\">\">Final Thoughts: Interactive Video for eLearning</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Training employees is an important part of a business. But the truth is tight budgets and deadlines can often get in the way of results. People can get demotivated, and with the<strong> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2019/apr/16/got-a-minute-global-attention-span-is-narrowing-study-reveals\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">short attention span becoming a real problem</a></strong>, it\'s important to take an efficient approach to learning in a corporate environment.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Using interactive videos for training employees is a step in the right direction and offers many benefits. What\'s more important is that it brings results while keeping the cost of training and learning from getting to an absurd level. It\'s a win-win for everyone!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>How Do I Make an Interactive Training Video?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The thought of creating an interactive training video might seem daunting at first, but if you follow the basic guidelines we talked about here, you should be fine. The first step is <strong><a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/blog-training-video-script-example/\">writing the video script</a></strong>, and you really don\'t want to rush that. Once you have that, the rest of the steps should come naturally.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3>What Are Some Examples of Interactive Video?</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Basically, any video that lets you interact with it in some capacity can be considered an interactive video. Non-interactive videos come with a couple of functions, such as stop, play, pause, rewind, fast forward, etc. But with an interactive video, you get to interact with the narrative itself in some way.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Black Mirror: Bandersnatch and Unbreakable Kimmy Schmidt: Kimmy vs. The Reverend are two great examples of interactive video content. For corporate learning or employee training, elements such as quizzes or branching videos are often used as interactive components.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you\'re looking for a complete eLearning solution for your business, give Ninja Tropic a try, we\'ll provide you with a commitment-free sample plan that meets your objectives.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Are you aware of the sheer power of engaging eLearning solutions but not sure where to start?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Schedule a free 30-minute consultation with a Ninja Tropic expert to analyze your association, university, or enterprise’s content objectives and map out the interactive blueprint to achieve them.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'Interactive Video for eLearning: How to Engage Learners & Boost Results', 'Unlock the power of interactive video learning to boost engagement and knowledge retention. Discover innovative strategies for impactful eLearning', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '2589-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-06-21 04:33:16', '2026-06-21 04:33:16', '', '2589', 'http://localhost:8080/?p=2813', '0', 'revision', '', '0'),
('2814', '0', '2026-06-21 04:33:21', '2026-06-21 04:33:21', '<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":1} -->
<h1>7 Microlearning Tips to Improve Learner Experience (2023 Strategy)</h1>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>While <a href=\"https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Tomas-Javorcik/publication/334401054_Results_of_Pilot_Study_into_the_Application_of_MicroLearning_in_Teaching_the_Subject_Computer_Architecture_and_Operating_System_Basics/links/5d278a51299bf1547cad2ddb/Results-of-Pilot-Study-into-the-Application-of-MicroLearning-in-Teaching-the-Subject-Computer-Architecture-and-Operating-System-Basics.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Polasek and Javorcik</a> (2019) proved the benefits of microlearning, you can’t simply introduce a microlearning system to your employees and let the platform do the job for you.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title1\">What Are the Benefits of Implementing a Microlearning Strategy?</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title2\">Top 7 Strategy Tips for Microlearning Content</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title3\">How to Get Started With Microlearning</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title4\">3 Potential Mistakes to Avoid With Microlearning</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title5\">Final Thoughts: Tips for an Effective Microlearning Strategy in 2023</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The platform itself will keep learners engaged and help them learn quickly. However, as the wisest before us said:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>\"There’s always room for improvement!\"</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>But how? What are the specifics you can look for to improve learner experience?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The goal is to have a solid microlearning strategy when you’re preparing the learning material. You can only do that when you have a clear idea of your learning objectives.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Also, if you want to make microlearning work for you, not against you, you need to monitor everything carefully.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In this article, we will give you 7 clever microlearning strategies to improve overall learning outcomes.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>So, let’s hop in…</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Simply put:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} -->
<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>Short and varied microlearning videos don’t stress the human attention span</li>
<li>Better retention due to short lectures and more learner participation</li>
<li>Easy to access from anywhere</li>
</ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Microlearning takes a different approach to knowledge by breaking down large course material into smaller bite-sized pieces.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As a result, instead of having to sit through a long (and boring) lecture, learners get to absorb short bursts of information.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In fact, microlearning has become the primary means of training employees in many organizations.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Here’s a detailed look at what microlearning can do for your organization:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>1. Improved Knowledge Retention</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Sitting through lectures or videos doesn’t necessarily mean that you are “learning.”</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"https://www.verywellmind.com/what-is-learning-2795332#:~:text=Learning%20Is%20an%20Active%20Process\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Learning is a process</a> that involves absorbing new information, retaining it, and reflecting upon it when needed.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And a proper microlearning strategy will allow the learners to retain the knowledge they gather more efficiently. Since the new information is delivered in small chunks, it’s easier to absorb for the learner.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>2. Cost and Time Efficient</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Setting up a digital learning structure to train your employees takes up company resources. And if you want to see results as early as possible, a proper <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/blog-how-to-write-a-microlearning-video-script-in-6-steps/\">microlearning strategy</a> is the best approach.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Compared to the traditional e-learning system, microlearning content, like courses, means less time and more efficiency.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>3. Fast Learning</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Learning takes time. But time’s an invaluable resource when you are running a business and <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/blog-how-to-plan-create-effective-employee-training-videos-step-by-step-guide/\">training your employees</a>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you need to spend a month educating your employees, your organization will take a hit.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>With a proper microlearning roadmap, you can minimize the time it takes for your workers to learn new information. Microlearning allows the learner to learn at their own pace and is often much faster than other learning methods.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>4. Better Learners Satisfaction</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2018/04/11/millennials-largest-generation-us-labor-force/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Millennials and GenZ</a> make up almost half the workforce in the US right now.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And with shorter attention spans becoming a real problem in the current generation, it’s difficult to design training materials that will ensure motivated learners are satisfied.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>With a proper strategy implemented during course creation, you can ensure your employees are fully satisfied with the learning experience. You can always <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/contact-us/\">seek professional help</a> regarding your business’s microlearning strategy if you’re not sure what to do.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Good learning content is from the learners, by the learners, and for the learners.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If your designed microlearning course cannot bring results, then it’s a clear indication that it’s not optimized for your employees.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>There are a few key elements to designing an efficient microlearning program. And while some of these elements may seem basic, failing to address them can lead to subpar learning results.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Let’s have a look…</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>1. Know Learners and Learning Objectives</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Sticking to a single <a href=\"https://bau.edu/blog/types-of-learning-styles/#:~:text=This%20model%20identifies%20four%20types,a%20complementary%20way%20of%20teaching.\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">learning style</a> can save you some time, but it won’t help you motivate your learners.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Everyone has different learning preferences. And to create an effective microlearning course, you need to address all your diverse learners.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Some learners respond better to spaced repetition, some have an easier time absorbing a quick video, and some even prefer focused quizzes. And you need to understand your learners to develop varied microlearning modules.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Set your sights on a specific learning outcome and create lessons that your learners respond to in small chunks to keep them engaged and interested.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>2. Create Milestones</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>\">\">Information served in a microlearning system is bite-sized, and you need to use that to your advantage.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Set small goals and objectives for your learners and set up small rewards that <a href=\"https://www.forbes.com/sites/forbescoachescouncil/2019/06/24/recently-succeed-at-something-celebrating-is-good-for-your-brain/?sh=6a823a093d91\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">celebrate</a> their achievements. Celebrating small achievements will give your employees a juicy dopamine hit that’ll keep them hooked on the training.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You might have an entire course planned, but the best approach is to focus on one learning objective at a time.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Break down a longer course into multiple small segments. Once your learner achieves a certain objective, they’d be able to move on to the next steps.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>3. Eliminate Distractions</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Creating microlearning content that focuses on a singular topic can be difficult.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>We often see educators mentioning additional elements that require the learners to divert from the preset path that’s laid out for them. And that can be a problem.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Giving learners a focused approach to new knowledge is essential for effective microlearning courses. When they are taking part in a specific concept, make sure they have all the resources and tools included in the content to know everything about it without having to search online.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You cannot deviate from the topic at hand. Failing to do so will distract the learners and can break the overall microlearning experience.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>4. Make it Engaging, Interesting & Fun</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>People learn better when they’re having fun and find the lesson engaging.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And if you’re designing a microlearning course aimed at learners’ satisfaction, you need to make the content interesting.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Employees in the current generation are often plagued with a shiny object syndrome. So it’s very easy for them to lose focus.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This means if you can’t create <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/blog-interactive-video-platforms-are-the-future-of-online-learning/\">interactive content</a> that keeps them interested and motivated, you won’t be able to achieve the company’s learning objective.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Consider adding animated text, <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/blog-microlearning-video/\">microlearning videos</a>, interactive quizzes, games, etc., as part of the course and keep your learners connected with the program.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You can even use real-world scenarios as a basis while designing the courses to give them relevant tasks and challenges.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>5. Optimize for Mobile Phones</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Did you know that people spend one-third of their <a href=\"https://www.bbc.com/news/technology-59952557\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">waking time on phones</a>?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>So, if you don’t utilize the power of mobile devices when you are creating microlearning courses, you’re making a big mistake!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>When designing <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/blog-how-to-storyboard-microlearning-videos/\">microlearning content</a>, it’s essential for educators to ensure it works on mobile platforms like smartphones, laptops, and tablets.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>For companies that have remote employees and workers, having mobile-friendly online content is essential for digital training.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Mobile learning, or <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/blog-what-is-mobile-learning-m-learning-benefits-tips/\">m-learning</a>, has become an integral part of microlearning and e-learning in general. With mobile-friendly microlearning content, your employees or students can engage with the material any time they want.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>6. Mix and Match Training Types</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Learning doesn’t always have to be online when you’re running a business.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Though it can take up a bit of company time and resources, it’s often a good idea to add a bit of in-person training to the program.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/what-is-blended-learning/\">The combination of mobile learning and in-house training</a> will help your employees achieve a better learning experience overall. And it also raises morale and motivation among the workforce.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>7. Analyze and Monitor Results</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Different <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/best-microlearning-platforms/\">microlearning platforms for corporate training</a> allow you to monitor and analyze user interaction through the dashboard.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You’ll be able to get insights like:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>Course completion rate<br /></li>
<li>How long it takes to complete a certain task<br /></li>
<li>How many employees take part in a course</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And the numbers are your friends.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>With the data that you gather by monitoring employee performance in a specific course, you can optimize the content to help your learners achieve better results.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Microlearning offers <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/benefits-of-microlearning/\">many benefits</a>, and well-organized training content that focuses on a singular topic can help you teach your employees with higher efficiency.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And shifting to a microlearning structure isn’t as hard as you might think.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Instead of completely redesigning the training materials in your organization, you can take your existing content and shrink it down into smaller digestible pieces.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If your old training consisted of hour-long videos or boring “click-next” presentations, you need to split it into multiple videos that last two to five minutes that discuss the same idea in a sequential way.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Remember: there’s no right or wrong way here. <a href=\"https://www.td.org/insights/just-how-micro-is-microlearning#:~:text=We%20found%20that%20the%20average%20maximum%20amount%20of%20time%20respondents%20reported%20that%20microlearning%20should%20be%20is%20about%2013%20minutes.%20However%2C%20the%20average%20amount%20of%20time%20participants%20said%20microlearning%20should%20ideally%20be%20is%2010%20minutes.%20%C2%A0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The average length of a microlearning</a> lesson is around 10 minutes. But, as long as you can keep it under 15 minutes, it can be classed as microlearning.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Instead of focusing on time limitations, what you need to think about is the learning objective. When designing a specific course roadmap, make sure you are achieving a result, or rather a learning goal, in each lesson.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As for the number of lessons per course – there’s no limit.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>But ideally, a maximum of ten lessons per course should be your target. If it takes more than that, then maybe you should consider breaking the lesson structure into more modules.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>With all that in mind, here are a couple of microlearning examples that you can add to a course:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>Short-form, animated text</li>
<li>Illustrations and Photos</li>
<li>Audiobooks and Music</li>
<li>Quizzes and other forms of tests</li>
<li>Interactive Games ‍with leaderboards</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you still feel confused or intimidated by the whole process, you can always get a free consultation from an <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/elearning-video-animation-companies-free-consultation/\">eLearning solutions provider</a> for clearer guidelines.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Bite-sized lessons are fun to absorb, but designing one can be pretty challenging. Here are three mistakes you want to avoid when creating a micro-lesson.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>1. Information Overload</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The first big mistake you want to avoid is putting too much information in a single lesson. Microlearning works best when the information is delivered in smaller chunks. And overloading your learners with too much information from the get-go will lead to subpar knowledge retention.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>\">\"><strong>2. Too Much Focus on the Clock</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Microlearning is supposed to be brief, but the time limit shouldn’t be your primary concern when planning a lesson.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>While it’s important to keep the lesson short and sweet, you should make sure you are giving your learners complete information on the topic. Going over the time limit is fine as long as it’s necessary.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>3. Sticking to a Single Format</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Your microlessons should include a good blend of materials for a complete learning experience. You shouldn’t stick to a single delivery format and instead mix and match videos, infographics, illustrations, and interactive elements in different lessons.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Experimentation is the key to figuring out how microlearning can work for you. That is true for all things in learning and design.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Take some time to see what works and what doesn’t. Don’t shy away from trying new things!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Our guidelines on microlearning strategies should give you a solid foundation to start designing your courses.<br />Itching to get started?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Book a <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/contact-us/\">free consultation</a> with us, and we’ll help you get in touch with the right eLearning solutions for your team.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Are you aware of the sheer power of engaging eLearning solutions but not sure where to start? Schedule a free 30-minute consultation with a Ninja Tropic expert to analyze your association, university, or enterprise’s content objectives and map out the interactive blueprint to achieve them.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', '7 Microlearning Tips to Improve Learner Experience (2023 Strategy)', 'Are microlearning tips a dime a dozen? Not with this new 2023 microlearning strategy. Incorporate this into your training and you&#8217;re good!', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '2591-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-06-21 04:33:21', '2026-06-21 04:33:21', '', '2591', 'http://localhost:8080/?p=2814', '0', 'revision', '', '0'),
('2815', '0', '2026-06-21 04:33:26', '2026-06-21 04:33:26', '<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":1} -->
<h1>Best Microlearning Platform for Corporate Learning (2023)</h1>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Looking for the best microlearning platforms in 2023?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title1\">What Are Microlearning Platforms?</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title2\">What To Look For in a Microlearning Platform</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title3\">11 Best Microlearning Platforms</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title4\">What are the Best Microlearning Platforms for Corporate Training in 2023?</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title5\">Final Thoughts: Best Platform for Corporate Learning in 2023</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title6\">Microlearning Platforms FAQ</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Before we talk shop, please have a look at these stats:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>TikTok users <a href=\"https://www.wired.co.uk/article/tiktok-wants-longer-videos-like-not\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">find videos longer</a> than 60 seconds stressful</li>
<li>Short-form videos popularity will soar in 2023, according to <a href=\"https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/hubspot-blog-marketing-industry-trends-report\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Hubspot</a></li>
<li>And <a href=\"https://www.forbes.com/sites/dbloom/2022/08/11/youtube-video-shorts-see-giant-jump-in-views-in-past-year/?sh=225b7b3133fc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">50% of YouTube views</a> are under 60 seconds (updated July 2022)</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Like it or not – this is a clear indication that human attention span has taken a big hit in recent years. So, if your business relies on once-tried-and-true training methods, it\'s likely to suffer.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>So, what\'s the solution?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Enter Microlearning Platforms.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>These platforms offer businesses and individuals the ability to take a smart approach to learning by breaking down existing content into small bite-sized pieces. As a result, <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/blog-how-to-plan-create-effective-employee-training-videos-step-by-step-guide/\">training employees</a> on new skills become much easier because they have more realistic knowledge checks.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And if you want to incorporate microlearning into your corporate L&D, exploring your options is always a great idea. That\'s why we\'ve decided to compare and talk about some of the best microlearning platforms for corporate learning.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Let\'s hop in!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>\"What\'s in a name?\"</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>While Shakespeare wanted to show that naming is irrelevant, when it comes to microlearning, it\'s all in the name.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Broken down to its very essence – micro = small, and learning = gaining knowledge.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>So, quick and small bursts of learning instead of the traditional consumption of a large chunk of information is microlearning.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Microlearning platforms can be mobile apps or websites that make learning content fun and engaging by:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>Creating bite-sized training material (<a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/blog-microlearning-video/\">videos</a>, texts, images)</li>
<li>Incorporating short quizzes to make the training process engaging</li>
<li>Gamifying learning content</li>
<li>And the one thing subpar microlearning platforms miss – having a very specific goal for each training</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The advantage of the microlearning approach is that learners can consume knowledge at a much quicker pace. A top-shelf microlearning platform makes learning fun and keeps learners hooked.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Online courses from microlearning platforms <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/benefits-of-microlearning/\">help businesses</a> in training their employees and capture new life skills by taking a path-based approach to learning. And more importantly, it also saves time and company resources.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Microlearning has come a long way since its conception. And with the \"<a href=\"https://time.com/3858309/attention-spans-goldfish/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Goldfish Effect</a>\" becoming a real problem, there\'s a risk of your employees getting lost or distracted in a maze of interactive content.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you want to get the most out of online training, you need to look for some essential features in your chosen microlearning platform.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Learning Curve </strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Software adoption can be a tough job for many individuals or even big businesses. Switching to a microlearning platform suddenly instead of the traditional process can take some time to get used to.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And if a microlearning app is hard to integrate into your business ecosystem, it\'s not going to do your employees any favors. That\'s why it\'s important to go with a platform that doesn\'t have a steep learning curve.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Time & Budget </strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You need to pick a platform that fits your budget and saves you time by delivering a complete library that you can use right away.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you want to make your own training courses, make sure you don\'t need to jump through a bunch of hoops to access simple features in the platform.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Current Software Setup</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you have an existing learning system for your employees, it\'s best to go with a platform that lets you build on it.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You don\'t want to throw away the material you already have.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Instead of taking a completely different approach to learning, all the best microlearning platforms enable you to improve upon existing content.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>LMS Features </strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>LMS, or Language Management System, is a digital environment to manage different training efforts.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And when you are choosing a platform to go with, you should look for LMS features like granular reporting, analytical capabilities, gamification, security, etc.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Goals & Objectives</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>What are you trying to get out of the platform or app?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>What\'s your desired end result?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Ask yourself these questions and try to figure out how a microlearning platform will help you achieve them.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And if you feel lost, you can always get a free consultation with an <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/elearning-video-animation-companies-free-consultation/\">eLearning solutions provider</a> to help you get back on track!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Microlearning is not free, and picking one platform that works for you can be hard if you don\'t do your homework. Here are some of the best platforms that are available for businesses and individuals.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} -->
<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li><strong><a href=\"https://www.edapp.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">EdApp</a></strong></li>
</ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>EdApp is your one-stop solution to online learning, whether you are looking to train your employees or publish course content. Features like multiple device support, template library, mobile app integration, and built-in games make this platform an attractive choice for anyone.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The platform also allows for social learning and peer learning features such as assignments, group discussions, practical assessments, etc.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Usability features in the platform include AI Translation, quiz maker, spaced repetition, deep links, and offline mode, among other things.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>Key features:</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>Impeccable customer support</li>
<li>A seamless blend of microlearning, <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/blog-what-is-mobile-learning-m-learning-benefits-tips/\">mobile learning</a>, peer learning, and gamification</li>
<li>Features like spaced repetition, rapid refresh, and group discussions can help the learners</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>EdApp offers four different pricing models with unique features as you go up a tier.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>Free (Free model): You don\'t pay anything but also don\'t get access to some of the important features. Biggest caveat – you need dedicated personnel to create the course content.</li>
<li>Do-It-Yourself ($2.95/month): Includes API integration, Artificial Intelligence aided translation, SSO, and many other features</li>
<li>Managed ($2.95-$5.95/month): Content produced by EdApp, additional account and onboarding support, comes with multiple plans</li>
<li>Enterprise (Custom): Dedicated account manager and onboarding support, <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/what-is-blended-learning/\">blended learning</a> plan, scalable production support<br /></li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} -->
<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li><strong><a href=\"https://www.ispringsolutions.com/ispring-learn\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">iSpring Learn</a></strong></li>
</ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>iSpring Learn as a platform lets you start developing microlearning content and track results with minimal hassle. You can use your existing videos, presentations, and slides to create content.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The biggest strength of this platform is the built-in authoring tool that lets you make responsive and engaging content with knowledge checks. And the smartphone app is also pretty intuitive.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>Clean and simple user interface</li>
<li>Allows easy monitoring of quiz and simulation reports, content reports, and email notifications.</li>
<li>Includes a powerful authoring tool for training</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>iSpring Learn offers two different pricing models, but the cost depends on how many users will have access.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>We suggest going through the <a href=\"https://www.ispringsolutions.com/ispring-learn/pricing\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">pricing page</a> to get a clearer idea about it. But for 500 users, your pricing options are:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>Start ($2.29/user/month): mobile apps with offline support, management automation, 50 GB storage, iSpring Suite authoring toolkit, etc.</li>
<li>Business ($3.14/user/month): iSpring Suite Max authoring toolkit with additional features, 360-degree performance appraisal, corporate portal, etc.<br /></li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} -->
<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li><strong><a href=\"https://www.edume.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">EduMe</a></strong></li>
</ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>EduMe is a mobile learning platform that utilizes a social-media-esque format to give users a seamless learning experience. It\'s easy, intuitive, and provides you with real-time data on the performance and productivity of your deskless workforce.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The integrated authoring tool allows you to quickly create training content in the form of microlearning courses, surveys, quizzes, videos, and more.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It promotes building a learning environment for your employees without getting in the way of their responsibilities.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>Message authoring tool</li>
<li>Includes a free microlearning course library</li>
<li>Allows monitoring of productivity and performance of the user groups</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>EduMe only offers a custom-tailored payment plan.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>So, we won\'t be able to give you an exact quotation. However, they do offer a free trial. So if you\'re on the fence about the platform, feel free to give it a go.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} -->
<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li><strong><a href=\"https://www.7taps.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">7taps</a></strong></li>
</ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Small businesses often rely on simple training materials to train their employees. With 7taps, you can get the power of digital training at your fingertips.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You can add images, videos, quizzes, and other engine content to create sequential course material intuitively in under 15 minutes.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Like most other platforms or microlearning software, the best features of this platform are hidden behind a paywall. But the free version of the platform is also an excellent choice for new users and startups.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>Has a well-rounded freemium model</li>
<li>Password-protected course creation for the Pro model and above</li>
<li>7taps AI support</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>7taps offers three different subscription models, and regardless of the one you go with, the user number is unlimited.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>Free (Free model): The free version of 7taps supports 1 shared course, 3 video uploads, 1 AI-video quiz/day, 7taps AI access, and more.</li>
<li>Pro ($99/month, $84/month for an annual subscription): The Pro version adds features like analytics and reporting, password-protected courses, and learning path along with increasing the number of video uploads, shared courses, etc.</li>
<li>Enterprise (Custom): The Enterprise plan adds more to the mix, such as XAPI and course export, Integration with HR systems, and User Management controls.</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} -->
<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li><strong><a href=\"https://www.ottolearn.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">OttoLearn</a></strong></li>
</ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The award-winning gamified learning approach of OttoLearn towards eLearning and knowledge retention makes them a top-tier platform for businesses and individuals. The smartphone app utilizes a clean and user-friendly UI.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The ability to analyze knowledge gaps in your employee through performance monitoring allows you to develop a content library that\'s specifically designed to optimize training delivery.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It also includes various integrations like rapid authoring, multilingual support, and interactive analytics, among other things.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>Requires no enrollments</li>
<li>Large, customizable content library</li>
<li>User-friendly mobile app</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>Ottolearn Provides a couple of different payment plans billed annually. The plans start at $250/month and offer a free demo for organizations looking to try it out.</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} -->
<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li><strong><a href=\"https://www.masteroapp.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Master-O</a></strong></li>
</ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Master-O is a productive platform that specializes in boosting sales and customer service. This platform works well for fields like healthcare, telecom, and banking industries.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You can use the interactive authoring tool in Master-O to repack your content into bite-sized online courses. The platform has an extensive library of sales training content to get you started immediately.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>Customizable sales training content</li>
<li>Clean and transparent UI</li>
<li>Video-based sales coaching</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>Master-O gives you a custom pricing plan for the number of users, which means we can\'t give you an exact quote. But you have the option to book a demo for free to try out their services before you commit to it.</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} -->
<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li><strong><a href=\"https://qstream.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Qstream</a></strong></li>
</ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Qstream is a simple and efficient platform. By gamifying the learning process, the platform can help employees learn new information.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You can use preexisting SCORM content or create your own path as you see fit.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The mobile app makes online courses fun to complete, and the push notifications let individuals access it the moment you create content.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Also, Qstream is integrated with other platforms like Frictionless, Slack, Microsoft, Webex, etc.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>Seamless UI makes it easy for even a beginner to use</li>
<li>Detailed analytics for insights into a learner\'s proficiency</li>
<li>Integration with various useful platforms</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>There\'s an option to try out the platform for free. If you like its features, you need to schedule a call to get a custom pricing plan.</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} -->
<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li><strong><a href=\"https://axonify.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">mLevel</a></strong></li>
</ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>mLevel is a data-driven digital learning platform that\'s used by some of the biggest companies in the world. As of March 2021, <a href=\"https://axonify.com/news/axonify-continues-to-scale-with-acquisition-of-digital-learning-platform-mlevel/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">mLevel is a part of Axonify</a>, which is a leading frontline employee training platform.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>mLevel is used by enterprises to train the frontline workforce on the use of software and policies and reinforces leadership skills.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Gamified content in the platform delivers an interactive learning experience for the workforce.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>Short daily exercises</li>
<li>A fully customizable content marketplace</li>
<li>Employee rewards system based on learner\'s score and performance on the platform</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>Since mLevel was acquired by Axonify, you need to book a call with the platform to get a custom plan based on your users and goals.</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} -->
<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li><a href=\"https://surge9.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Surge9</strong></a></li>
</ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Surge9 is a \"mobile-first\" platform. Now mobile first can mean a lot of things, but for Surge9, it means that the app is written directly on iOS and Android OS. As a result, it can utilize the full capabilities of a smartphone giving you fast and responsive UI and, most importantly, offline access.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Apart from that, Surge9 is also powered by AI technology giving you access to advanced analytics, gamification, easy content authoring, multiple languages compatibility, and more.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>Easy content authoring features to create your own path to learning</li>
<li>AI-Powered microlearning</li>
<li>Fast and responsive UI even when you\'re offline</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>Surge9 follows two different payment models. You can either get it on a per-user per year basis or per-user per month basis. But since it follows the SaaS model, you need to contact them to get an exact quote.</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} -->
<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li><strong><a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/in/app/shotclasses/id1080943112\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ShotClasses</a></strong></li>
</ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>ShotClasses is a mobile-only platform, available for <a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/in/app/shotclasses/id1080943112\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">iOS</a> and <a href=\"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.mindtree.shotclasses&hl=en_IN\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Android</a>, that lets you create microlessons using SCORM, videos, PDFs, presentations, and more, quickly and with minimal hassle.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Some noteworthy features include building quizzes, monitoring feedback, gamification, and peer-to-peer learning.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>Dedicated cloud storage with 99% uptime</li>
<li>Create learning materials quickly using different sources</li>
<li>24/7 email and mobile support</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>Since this platform mostly deals with organizations and enterprises, there\'s no specific pricing model available for it. You need to contact MindTree and create a custom plan that\'s tailored to your specific situation.</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} -->
<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li><strong><a href=\"https://www.talentcards.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TalentCards</a></strong></li>
</ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>While most of the microlearning software and solutions cater to a wide variety of employees, TalentCards focuses specifically on frontline or field workers. It\'s a mobile platform and uses a flashcard approach to learning.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Creating content is easy and can be done in three simple steps.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Firstly, create a card set with your selected material.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Add users and send an invite link to download the app.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Then share your card set with your employees so that they can access it on their smartphones.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>Easy content creation tool</li>
<li>Supports in-app branding and push notifications</li>
<li>A well-rounded freemium model</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>TalentCards offers three different pricing models.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>Free (Free model up to 5 users): Multiple content support, spaced repetition, offline access, unlimited courses, etc.</li>
<li>Standard ($50/month up to 50 users): Video upload and storage, custom feedback, Public API, and more built on top of all the features in the Free model.</li>
<li>Premium ($75/month up to 50 users): Everything in the free and standard model in addition to Automated notifications, activity log, teams, and a Success Manager.</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>While there are many amazing microlearning platforms out there that let you create or learn content efficiently, not all of them are good for a corporate framework.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In a corporate scenario, certain features, such as integration with HR systems, blended learning plans, and advanced analytics, become much more important.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you don\'t have a clear idea about the sort of learning environment you want to introduce in your corporate structure, talking to <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/contact-us/\">an eLearning solutions</a> team should help you figure out the best approach.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>With that said, two of the most popular platforms for corporate training today are 7taps and EdApp. There are other options out there, but these two are at the top of the ladder.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>People have shorter attention spans now. And in the corporate world, where picking up new skills is important for an employee, breaking down large chunks of knowledge into digestible bits can be extremely useful.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>These platforms let you utilize the power of digital learning and help your employees grasp different skills without sacrificing their responsibilities.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Hopefully, this article on the best platforms for corporate learning could help you find the perfect tool for your business.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And of course, if you need <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/elearning-video-animation-companies-free-consultation/\">help with any of your learning needs</a>, we\'d be happy to help!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":2} -->
<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How to Make the Most of Microlearning Training</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Is a Microlearning Platform Essential to Deliver Training?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>While a microlearning platform isn\'t absolutely essential to deliver training to your employees, it can make the overall process a lot smoother.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Many companies are opting to switch to a microlearning structure to help their workforce acquire skills quickly.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><strong>What Is the Difference Between eLearning and Microlearning?</strong></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>eLearning platforms offer an online course in a structured \"long-form\" way, sort of what you would see in universities. That means <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/blog-why-video-based-learning-is-a-must-for-corporate-elearning/\">eLearning</a> courses typically contain long videos, sometimes lasting 4 or 5 hours.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Microlearning, on the other hand, breaks down specific content into small units to make it easier for the learner to absorb and understand. Usually, a microlearning online course contains short videos, images, presentations, and other learning materials.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Is Microlearning Effective?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Yes, microlearning is highly effective at delivering focused training to employees without getting in the way of complex workflows in a corporate environment.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Instead of going through long and tedious video lectures, microlearning takes a smarter approach by breaking it down into small pieces that are easier to understand.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Are you aware of the sheer power of engaging eLearning solutions but not sure where to start? Schedule a free 30-minute consultation with a Ninja Tropic expert to analyze your association, university, or enterprise’s content objectives and map out the interactive blueprint to achieve them.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->', 'Best Microlearning Platforms for Corporate Learning (2023)', 'Explore the best microlearning platforms to enhance your training programs. Find the top solutions for engaging, efficient, and effective learning.', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '2593-revision-v1', '', '', '2026-06-21 04:33:26', '2026-06-21 04:33:26', '', '2593', 'http://localhost:8080/?p=2815', '0', 'revision', '', '0'),
('2816', '0', '2026-06-21 04:33:30', '2026-06-21 04:33:30', '<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":1} -->
<h1>5 Benefits of Microlearning for Businesses & Non-Profit Organizations</h1>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Let’s be honest, the benefits of microlearning for both businesses and non-profit organizations are vast. In today’s busy and chaotic society, we’re busier than ever before.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In fact, interruptions disrupt our focus anywhere between <a href=\"https://www.spica.com/blog/interruptions-at-work\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">4 to 12 times every hour</a>. Whether it’s self-imposed or external, these interruptions take around <a href=\"https://today.duke.edu/2021/11/3-ways-bounce-back-after-work-interruption\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">23 minutes</a> on average to get back on track.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title1\">What is Microlearning?</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title2\">3 Key Principles of<br /> Microlearning</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title3\">5 Benefits of Microlearning</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title4\">Who Benefits from<br /> Microlearning?</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title5\">What Are Some Examples of<br /> Microlearning?</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title6\">Are There Any Disadvantages of<br /> Microlearning?</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"#title7\">How to Make the Most of<br /> Microlearning Training</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>That’s why microlearning training is so essential.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>It replaces the old “click next” slide presentations that eat away at our time without the benefit of increased engagement, knowledge retention, or behavioral change that comes from short-burst microlearning modules.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>How does this help businesses and nonprofits make lasting changes to their corporate training and learning culture?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Let’s get into it!</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Before we get into the nitty gritty of microlearning benefits for your organization, let’s first get a deeper understanding of what <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/blog-microlearning-video/\">microlearning</a> is and how it’s defined.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Simply put:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Microlearning courses and other online training methods help the learner by providing training in small incremental bursts that provide focus and clarity.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Keeping the training programs short and concise allows for learner engagement to improve and provides many other benefits as well.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Each microlearning video can allow for the concentration of a single learning objective to take place via just-in-time learning that permits learners to go at their own pace and incrementally build on their learning.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This is done with microlearning modules that either act as a standalone training, small parts of the whole learning objective, or, in many cases, both can be accomplished to provide autonomy to the training recipient.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Ok so now that we understand microlearning in a general sense, let’s cover some key principles that make microlearning so effective. Here are three essential components of microlearning that improve engagement.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li><strong>Quick Bursts of Education</strong></li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>One key component of microlearning is that the content should deliver learning objectives in short bursts. This varies depending on who you ask, but a good rule of thumb is to keep your videos under 10 minutes.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This helps traditional eLearning courses provide quality education via online learning that isn’t overwhelming.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li><strong>Accessible (Mobile) Learning</strong></li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Yet another principle that is paramount to effective microlearning programs is <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/blog-using-508-accessibility-tools-for-color-contrast-in-elearning-videos/\">accessibility</a>. Using <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/blog-what-is-mobile-learning-m-learning-benefits-tips/\">mobile learning</a> and other delivery methods helps learners achieve specific knowledge via online training.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This means that they can access microlearning content anywhere at any time on their own schedule. This level of autonomy is precisely what makes this learning technique so successful in today’s busy society.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li><strong>Microlearning Courses Use a Variety of Media</strong></li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Microlearning isn’t just a learning strategy, it’s a way of life for a lot of knowledge workers, businesses, and organizations. As such, this principle doesn’t just apply to one form of media.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Microlearning includes content delivery methods via a variety of mixed media such as images, text, videos, quizzes, games, and many more. Most of them include an interactive component and the most successful forms of microlearning media are audio-visual.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Even this post you’re reading now can be considered microlearning content.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Ok here we are, we have arrived.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>What microlearning benefits can you take advantage of as it applies to your organization? As we said earlier, the benefits are vast and there are too many to list, but here are the five most important benefits of adopting a microlearning strategy.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li><strong>Highly Engaging Learning Process</strong> One microlearning benefit is that it actually enhances learner engagement. This means that using proper microlearning techniques in your online training, such as inclusion and interactivity, will allow for focus and engagement to take place naturally. This is as opposed to traditional e-learning or face-to-face environments that are long and drawn out and can be considered bland or boring. Fragmented learning will create a highly focused and engaged learning process for personal and professional development.</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li><strong>Increased Knowledge Retention</strong></li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>What happens when your focused and engaged instead of zoning out thinking about what’s for dinner?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Any guesses?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You retain more of the information. In fact, learning modules that use a microlearning strategy and break training down into bite-sized chunks <a href=\"https://thrivemyway.com/microlearning-stats/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">increase long-term retention by 80%.</a></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>That’s quite the difference.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li><strong>Microlearning is More Affordable</strong> One incredible microlearning benefit is that microlearning development can have a positive effect on your bottom line. How so? Well, by eliminating recurring costs, classroom equipment, travel expenses, and in-person instructors, you’re able to increase your return on your time and money. In fact, <a href=\"https://www.arist.co/post/microlearning-research-benefits-and-best-practices\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">one learning expert</a> suggests that microlearning allows organizations to develop eLearning up to 300% faster while cutting development costs in half.</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li><strong>Provides Autonomy (and Freedom) to Learners</strong></li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Some of the key principles of microlearning allow for another benefit to take effect:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The mere fact that learning can take place from anywhere on any device at the convenience of the learner creates a real sense of freedom. This increases the level of satisfaction, happiness, and morale throughout the organization.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And happy learners make efficient employees and managers.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li><strong>Incredibly Efficient</strong> All these microlearning benefits add up to one very important benefit imperative to all organizations: Operational efficiency. When you have online education that cuts costs, gives you a higher return on your time, and gives employees autonomy to learn faster and more effectively, you have a recipe for success. And that success provides growth and scalability.</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The many benefits of microlearning can be enjoyed from all angles. Whether you’re a small business, a Fortune 500 company, or a non-profit organization, there’s something for everyone.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The main benefactors are the employees, customers, clients, and donors that receive the training, however.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This is because they can engage with a microlearning course via many different forms of interactive media to obtain a specific learning outcome.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Whether that’s <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/safety-training/\">safety training</a> for employees, <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/blog-product-knowledge-training-everything-you-need-to-know/\">product knowledge training</a> for customers, or an overview of mission objectives for donors.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In any case, adult learners can go at their own pace, prevent cognitive overload, and fill knowledge gaps in just a few minutes.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This pales in comparison to traditional training models.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>Microlearning Benefits for Businesses</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The benefits of microlearning content for businesses, corporations, and for-profit companies boil down to a few things…</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Efficiency, cost savings, and training autonomy.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Having the ability to access microlearning courses from any device on your own time, and implementing a mobile learning culture allows you to create efficient systems that save you precious time and money.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>That means you invest in some instructional design, a learning management system, and a few pieces of equipment and materials once for each course.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This allows you to cut out the unnecessary expenses of multiple recurring costs. Want to save even more? <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/elearning-video-animation-companies-free-consultation/\">Hire a professional eLearning agency</a> and save your resources to benefit from economies of scale.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In any case, you’re streamlining your training operations while increasing your bottom line.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>Microlearning Benefits for Non-Profits</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>What about the benefits of microlearning for non-profit organizations, <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/associations/\">associations</a>, or <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/universities/\">universities</a>? How might they benefit from the efficiency of learning management systems?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Well, first we need to ask ourselves, what is the main challenge for non-profits?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"https://designbycosmic.com/insights/articles/biggest-challenges-for-nonprofits/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Research shows</a> that the answer is unequivocally steady income stability, sustainability, and retention & engagement of donors.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>These common challenges have one thing in common:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li><strong>Messaging.</strong></li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Most non-profits fail to:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} -->
<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>Provide consistent messaging that educates potential donors about their cause, and…</li>
<li>How it connects, lands, and impacts their audience on an emotional level.</li>
<li>There is no follow-up after onboarding a donor.</li>
</ol>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In other words, there are operational inconsistencies when it comes to attracting, educating, nurturing, and retaining donors.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>How can microlearning help with that?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>By using short burst microlearning content, like videos, to inform and educate how your cause is making an impact, you can create meaningful connections that, statistically, improve engagement.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This creates a certain level of trust, openness, and receptiveness to future messages. This means, there <strong>must</strong> be future messages to nurture, indoctrinate, and retain donors.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>So we’ve discussed various microlearning benefits, but how can you put some of this training into action?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Well here are a few examples of microlearning that can be used in place of traditional elearning or workplace training.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>Interactive Videos</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>eLearning videos are our bread and butter. It’s just what we do. But long-form <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/video-animation/\">video animation</a> and live-action videos, like the type you see on <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a>, are not all great examples of microlearning.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>For it to qualify, you must have the elements of engagement and retention as well as bite-sized videos and accessibility. To do that, we incorporate <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/blog-interactive-video-platforms-are-the-future-of-online-learning/\">interactive videos</a> by adding quizzes, branched videos, gamification, and much more.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>And that is what makes for an excellent example of microlearning.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>Microlearning Applications</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Here’s another one:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>quick-hit learning modules you can do from anywhere that many companies incorporate into their mobile applications.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><a href=\"https://www.duolingo.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Duolingo</a> for example, allows you to go through a series of language training exercises you can do in a matter of minutes.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li>Short-Form Video</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Social media these days is growing exponentially in popularity.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Particularly, short-form video platforms like Tiktok, Instagram Stories, YouTube Shorts, and Twitter Moments are all great examples of microlearning in action.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If your company requires a social media presence, this can be a great way to transition into adopting a microlearning culture.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>What about the disadvantages of microlearning? Do they exist?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Sure, they do. Everything has pros and cons, right?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Here are a few disadvantages of microlearning training:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">
<li><strong>Paradox of Choice. </strong>Since microlearning is predicated on short bursts of training, this leaves a LOT of content to manage. It also creates the ability to have multiple topics with various content for each one available. Add to that the fact that there are many choices for content delivery and it can cause indecision for some learners.</li>
<li><strong>Limited Complexity. </strong>Microlearning isn’t the perfect solution for any and all types of training. For example, if you’re trying to train topics that are extremely complex, like surgery techniques, other methods of learning may make more sense.</li>
<li><strong>Requirement of Technology. </strong>The reality is that microlearning requires technology to be useful. Without it, the benefits can’t occur. This isn’t the end of the world, however, since in today’s day and age, most people have access to multiple devices or can gain access with little or no complications.</li>
</ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The question is: Do the pros outweigh the cons?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>This is a matter of opinion, but we’d like to think so. The sheer amount of microlearning benefits one can receive and the impact they have makes it an obvious choice for which direction to go.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>The benefits of microlearning have a clear impact on personal growth and development as well as the efficiency of your professional organization. It helps support on-the-job training, HR departments, non-profit donor retention, and so much more.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Traditional learning is a thing of the past. It’s time to modernize your organization and change with the times. Are you prepared for that?</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Make the most of your microlearning training. <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/contact-us/\">Contact Ninja Tropic</a> today for a free consultation to see how we can create a modern learning culture that allows your organization to improve its efficiency. Or for other elearning methods and DIY ideas, visit the <a href=\"https://www.ninjatropic.com/blog/\">Ninja Tropic Blog</a>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

