<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)</strong></h2>



<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>What is the difference between an AMS and an Association LMS?</strong></h3>



<p>An AMS (Association Management System) acts as your central hub for administrative tasks like membership data, dues, events, and communications. An Association LMS is a dedicated hub strictly for delivering education, tracking credentials, and fostering learning experiences. When tightly integrated, the AMS manages <em>who</em> your members are, while the LMS manages <em>how</em> they grow.</p>



<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Why shouldn&#8217;t our association just use a corporate LMS?</strong></h3>



<p>Corporate LMS tools are primarily designed for captive employees and focus heavily on mandatory compliance training. Association platforms are tailored for voluntary members, supporting complex non-dues revenue models, lifelong learning across career arcs, and fostering community. Opting for a corporate LMS can severely limit your ability to manage non-dues revenue and dynamic membership structures.</p>



<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>How does video content improve the LMS experience for members?</strong></h3>



<p>Video content caters to time-starved professionals who need efficient, bite-sized information they can apply immediately. Utilizing short, scenario-based videos not only builds emotional connection but also helps create personalized learning pathways—such as targeted welcome videos—that make members feel supported from day one.</p>
