<!-- wp:column -->
<div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Design FAQ</strong></h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>What does eLearning typically cost?</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><p>The cost of eLearning can vary depending on the complexity and length of the content. We offer flexible pricing to match your training needs, whether you—re looking for a simpleonline  course or a fully immersive, multimedia experience.</p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>As a cost leader in the industry, we—ve been able to provide exceptional value to our clients by leveraging our experience working with service associations, nonprofits, and as a backend studio to major agencies.n</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Our mission-driven approach ensures that we are committed to providing high-quality, affordable training solutions. For an hour of content, our prices typically range from $7,000 to $24,000 depending on the style and complexity of the online course.n</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->
<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>What makes a good design for learning?</strong></h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p><p>A good learning design is one that’s learner-centered, engaging, and results-driven. It should focus on practical applications, ensuring that learners can apply their knowledge and skills in real-world settings. Learning has to shift attitudes and inspire behavior change. Slides-based learning modules or poorly put together content do not communicate a positive message.</p></p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>
<!-- /wp:column --></div>
